{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs","id":1548575,"title":"Running the Free States - 4 - Canon Gangs & NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-18T17:52:46-08:00","id":1548575,"title":"Running the Free States - 4 - Canon Gangs & NPCs","content":"This thread is for discussion of actual canon gangs and NPCs from Los Angeles By Night sourcebook and other media (other sourcebooks, Bloodlines and other video games, etc.)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a> wanted someplace to comment <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1485320-anarch-domains-why-official-supplements-ignore-them\">on this thread</a> from several years ago where I first laid out some of my ideas on making the Free States more interesting. I'll be using some of those ideas in my own actual chronicle I'm currently planning. But people are free to discuss any canon characters or coteries, and can take them in different directions than I indicated.<br /> <br /> The Los Angeles metropolitan area can hold something like 150-170 vampires per the typical rule, and if you consider an anarch domain likely has even more, there's immense number of NPCs. Of course, PCs won't run into every single one. A lot of vampires will just be window dressing. So I'm making a list of concepts I like from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> thread on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates\">pre-made character templates found here</a>. It is an easy way to create a lot of instant characters whenever I need some random vampire characters. I'm not using all the templates, and I'm adjusting them as needed like changing clans since I need a lot more Brujah and Caitiff than I would for most domains.<br /> <br /> =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff\">Part 10 - Oddballs</a>\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  adding links 08-01-2025, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T13:45:09-08:00","id":1548599,"title":"","content":"- MOSEYS ON IN -<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy thank you kindly for the consideration, my good fox.\u201d<br /> <br /> - TIPS HAT -<br /> <br /> \u201cMuch appreciated.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T14:51:42-08:00","id":1548601,"title":"","content":"Anyway, that little reminder of my nom-de-plume\u2019s origins aside, I\u2019m a little later than one meant to be posting my first notion for a canon, but hitherto un-described character with connections to LA in particular and the Free States in general. <br /> <br /> So, in lieu of anybody you\u2019ve actually heard of, I proudly present to you -<br /> <br /> COUNT RIGATONI<br /> <br /> - The Tenth Generation Malkavian with my favourite name in VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE, the lick directly responsible for creating Bela aka Hollywood Dracula (AKA my favourite gonzo character in all Los Angeles) is described as someone who (In AD 1956) dressed up in the Classic movie vampire costume (Complete with cape and possibly-affected Hungarian accent), approached a first-class Bela Lugosi impersonator, offered to make him the Prince of Darkness and then proceeded to do just that (Whether the man actually said \u201cYes\u201d at any point remains a riddle lost to the ages), at the low, low price of driving the poor man quite insane.<br /> <br /> - With that in mind, it occurred to me that if \u2018Bela\u2019 is explicitly<br /> built as THE Classic Movie Vampire, it might be fun to depict his sire as someone completely obsessed with Movie Vampires (and, to an only slightly lesser extent, vampire movies): somebody who adopts a series of guises very deliberately modelled on Classic (or at least popular) movie vampires and thereby offers us, somewhat in the style of a miner\u2019s canary, an insight into how Pop Culture\u2019s conception of vampires changed and evolved over the decades (Whilst never quite escaping the long shadow left by what arguably remains THE Iconic screen Dracula).<br /> <br /> - My mental image is of an American with immigrant parents (The name \u2018Rigatoni\u2019 is Italianate, with specifically-Sicilian antecedents, but since it suggests a pasta dish and not any kind of Patrician, I\u2019m assuming that \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 is very, very not Italian: I\u2019m tempted to make him an Irish-American as a nod to Mr Bram Stoker\u2019s Irish roots) who was embraced by a Malkavian circa AD 1920 (A nod to the year in which Mr Bela Lugosi himself reached the USA) by a sire who took an interest in his career, but did something less than a bang-up job of selling their Childe on the lifestyle.<br /> <br /> - To say that the usual painful introduction to Kindred society (Coupled with the compelling, but not very attractive, vision of Graf Orlock in NOSFERATU) left the future \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 with somewhat melancholic tendencies would be putting things mildly: doing his best to soldier on regardless, Our Hero \u2026 well, our subject \u2026 cut his teeth, figuratively and literally, then went in search of an inspiration to carry him through the rest of his half-life existence.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll give you two guesses where he found it and the first one doesn\u2019t count (No pun intended).<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>DIGRESSION: As a further nod to Mr Bram Stoker, I\u2019m tempted to make the character\u2019s birth name something like \u2018Isaac\u2019 or \u2018Jacob\u2019 (Abraham - Isaac - Jacob).</i><br /> <br /> <br /> - Given the infinitely more glamorous vision of Mr Bela Lugosi smouldering away on the Big Screen (Also, THE BRIDES!) the newly-dubbed \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 went All In on emulating the accent, the style, the smoulder and then did his best to find a town where he could live his Best Life as a European expat doing his best to avoid the attempted extirpation of the aristocracy on that continent.<br /> <br /> It seldom worked for very long, but it usually worked just long enough to cheer him up and get him an entree into the more good-humoured elements of Kindred society (Note: it\u2019s possible that \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 originally settled in Los Angeles because Don Sebastian was one of the few Camarilla princes inclined to treat him as a Court Jester, rather than an incitement to breach of the Masquerade - Cocaine by proxy is one Hell of a drug).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Given a new lease on life when the Free States were established (If only because the Anarchs were rather less systematic about enforcing potential Masquerade breaches and, it should be said, because \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 had been in LA long enough to relax his persona a notch or two, our subject attempted to return the favour when he learned that his onscreen idol was at Death\u2019s Door, racing to extend the Embrace.<br /> <br /> Whether he found Bela Lugosi in no fit state to be considered for vampirism or genuinely confused a high-quality imitator for the man himself remains unclear (Bela\u2019s memory is \u2026 well, anyway, \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 will neither confirm nor deny, but he transformed his only known Childe within 24 hours of Bela Lugosi\u2019s death and that\u2019s all we know).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Their relationship in the years since remains \u2026 complicated.<br /> <br /> For one thing, whenever the two of them are together \u2018Bela\u2019 tends to treat \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 as his very own Renfield (\u2018Rigatoni\u2019 enjoys this treatment in surprisingly large doses, but does not have an infinite capacity for being Star-struck): for another, \u2018Rigatoni\u2019 tends to bring out those deeply, deeply repressed memories in \u2018Bela\u2019 which make things quite unpleasant for everybody in the vicinity (Especially Hollywood Dracula himself).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also the small, but significant detail that the two tend to be very, very obvious when together (and Count Rigatoni, not being a \u2018National Treasure\u2019 of the Anarch Free States, therefore tends to be sent off on his travels after a certain point, sometimes even quite peacefully).<br /> <br /> <br /> - When NOT coming to worship at the feet of The Master, \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 can usually be found keeping his cursed melancholies at bay by adopting the latest Pop Culture vampire trend (Usually, though not invariably, from the big screen), adapting his persona to match said trend, and finding some out-of-the-way pitch to pass himself off as the inspiration for (Rather than inspired by) that trend.<br /> <br /> While these efforts sometimes prove abortive, often enough they allow him to make a life in the local vampire community, generally allowing him to relax the persona into something a bit more naturalistic than affected (Sometimes for years at a time): in the end, however, the depressive (Arguably self-destructive) tendency gnaws away at his contentment - resulting in him either doubling down on his current persona until forced to flee or abandoning the persona and heading back to study at The Master\u2019s feet once more (For some reason Hollywood Dracula always, always cheers him up), seeking further inspiration along the way.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 is not meant to be a \u2018Fish Malk\u2019 (He adopts these many variations on his deeply theatrical persona not for his own amusement or as part of a delusion, but as a coping mechanism intended to lend a little glamour to the fairly bleak lifestyle of the Kindred or allow him an escape from his own gnawing insecurities): he is, however, an Anarch (If only by virtue of the Camarilla having a much lower tolerance for his theatrics and the Sabbat having quite possibly the least friendly sense of humour in the World of Darkness) and can reliably be found in the vicinity of the Anarch Free States (All the better to provide an escape route).<br /> <br /> He\u2019s an eccentric, but he\u2019s not crazy stupid.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, it should be noted that \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 bears a striking resemblance to Mr Peter MacNicol, a leading cause of his tendency to (A) periodically question his fitness as a vampire (B) devolve to the role of Vampire Renfield when in proximity to \u2018Bela\u2019 (C) Get into fights with those who take his attempts to embody the latest Hollywood Vampire trends exactly as seriously as they deserve, but fail to do so with any discretion.<br /> <br /> Given he\u2019s still alive after many, many, many of these fights, \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 may be more dangerous than he looks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-19T14:59:03-08:00","id":1548602,"title":"","content":"N.B. I\u2019m assuming that - given his love of Vampire Fiction and general interest in being the Perfect Vampire, \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 has a surprisingly-extensive knowledge of vampire lore (Which may make him an excellent \u2018spotter\u2019 when it comes to a vampire seeking to conceal their identity behind some obscure reference and a valuable resource when trying to puzzle out the weakness of a more potent foe); I\u2019m also fond of the notion that his commitment to theatricality, obsession with the \u2018Ideal\u2019 vampire and a certain amount of raw Ham make him surprisingly well-qualified to serve as a Harpy (Cutting overinflated egos down to size almost as ruthlessly as he surveys his own faults).<br /> <br /> Also, it deeply amuses me to imagine him as an old associate of Los Angeles\u2019 very own \u2018Surf Baron\u2019 (One imagines that the latter\u2019s commitment to making vampirism Fun is pure balm on Count Rigatoni\u2019s frequently-troubled soul).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T00:32:17-08:00","id":1548610,"title":"","content":"I don't have LA by Night handy and it has been too long since I last looked at it, but was there ever a gang/coterie based around surfers and adjacent LA/SoCal subcultures? The sort of thing that might've started back in the day off all those beach movies with Frankie, Annette, and Gidget, and evolving though Tom Wolfe's The Pumphouse Gang, the Z-Boys, Muscle Beach, and up to Point Break. Because it feels like the sort of thing that Vampire's LA should have. Especially if their leader is some sort of charismatic guru in the vein of Patrick Swayze in Point Break crossed with Keiffer Sutherland in The Lost Boys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T03:16:26-08:00","id":1548611,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a>, I believe that Free States LA <i>does</i> boast a Surfer Dude Baron - a Brujah, if memory serves, though one could also imagine a Toreador with an eye for athletics getting caught up with the \u2018Aqua Licks\u2019.<br /> <br /> I recall <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> mentioning that he didn\u2019t see the \u2018Surf Baron\u2019 as an actual Baron, <i>per se</i> - just the ringleader of a coterie (Possibly including the aforesaid \u2018Aqua Toreador\u2019).<br /> <br /> Part of the reason I\u2019m very grateful to him for creating this thread is that I wanted to push the notion that, while \u2018Brujah Bodhi\u2019 might not run an organised Barony (Insofar as Anarchs are ever organised), it\u2019s conceivable that as the \u2018Big Kahuna\u2019 of the Surf-and-Turf vampires in LA and spokesperson of the \u2018Sleep all day, party all night, never grow old\u2019 Kindred (Not to mention an extremely popular, charismatic dude) he can wield influence and put together a posse that - especially when other Anarch leaders are talking \u2018Big Time\u2019 rather than \u2018Fun Time\u2019 - effectively allows him to function as a Baron, at least for short periods of time.<br /> <br /> Even if (on a night-to-night basis) he functions as a dude with a coterie \u2018and a whole lotta friends\u2019, rather than a Baron (Especially if the coterie itself frequently serves as a hard core around which a floating population of casuals can condense into a bloc).<br /> <br /> Basically, if anywhere in the world can produce a \u2018part time baron, full time spokesman, party time dude\u2019 it\u2019s the Anarch Free States (and I think that could be a dynamic worth exploring, in terms of the unusual fluidity of the arrangement).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T09:20:29-08:00","id":1548616,"title":"","content":"N.B. Looking up the relevant details, the character in question is Steve Booth - who appears to have been Embraced in AD 1965 (Born in 1942, he might well have been almost exactly of the generation that made those \u2018Beach Blanket\u2019 movies).<br /> <br /> His direct \u2018family\u2019 tie to Crispus Attucks through their mutual sire Marguerite (and less direct tie to Marguerite\u2019s beau Jeremy MacNeil) might well explain his surprising status in LA Kindred circles (Along with what appears to be strong native charisma).<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m wonder if \u2018Brother\u2019 Crispus has ever taken up Steve\u2019s offer to take him surfing (It amuses me to imagine that Steve calls a remarkable number of people \u2018brother\u2019, but only Crispus seems to take it as an actual family dynamic rather than a verbal tic).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Marguerite Focart\u2019s role in the establishment of the Free States and her ties to at least three of the more noteworthy Kindred in the region strongly suggest she merits a place in LOS ANGELES BY NIGHT (My read is that she\u2019s a devoted Anarch, but otherwise something of a wild card).<br /> <br /> Also, Marguerite absolutely HAS gone surfing with Steve at one point: how well that particular experiment went I leave to the individual imagination.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Also, is there any description of the \u2018Lord Stanhope\u2019 mentioned as her third Childe, but not given a full write-up? (The name makes me think of a Victorian aristo with a strong hint of Tarzan - possibly an explorer whom Marguerite found wounded unto death, since the lady\u2019s approach to First Aid seems to be \u2018Kill the patient, then persuade them to stand back up).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m hoping he\u2019s the \u2018Black Sheep\u2019 of the brood (A committed adherent of the Camarilla and a Brujah of the most philosophical sort).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":". 02-20-2025, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T09:54:22-08:00","id":1548618,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, looking over your article on BLOODLINES characters in the \u2018Anarch domains\u2019 thread, it\u2019s interesting to note that his sire appears to have been a female Malkavian committed to his asylum and that his Embrace appears to have gone unnoticed for some years (Suggesting that his Sire was either ignored or something of an unknown quantity) before he was approached by the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s also amusing to note that the game\u2019s scriptwriters (either accidentally or on purpose) invented a new technique of medical (Psychological?) analysis called \u2018dactopintalosm\u2019 (With the name suggesting some sort of \u2018phrenology for fingers).<br /> <br /> With that in mind, it\u2019s easy to suspect he might have been an old Victorian and that his sire may well have been one of the first Malkavians in the LA region (Which, coupled with his apparent preference for ghouls over childer, might help explain why the Clan of Mad Oracles has a relatively minor presence in the area).<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, the significant period of time between his Embrace and his acceptance into the Camarilla may help explain his survival of the Second Anarch Revolt - he wasn\u2019t part of the Don Sebastian regimen for long enough to become a target (One can only wonder if he was spared, despite being an apparently-spontaneous Embrace, because either somebody in Don Sebastian\u2019s service or the Don himself believed that having an in-house medical expert might help the Prince of LA cope with his alleged substance abuse issues).<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, it\u2019s downright <i>hilarious</i> to imagine such a solemnly Gothic and Science-minded Malkavian being obliged to deal with a Clan-mate (and for all we know a Brood-mate) willing to dub himself \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 and downright <i>eager</i> to embrace Bela Lugosi as the REAL Prince of Darkness.<br /> <br /> \u2018Bela\u2019 he can deal with as a broken mind in the grip of a fiercely upheld delusion, but \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 does what he does by <i>choice</i>, as a coping mechanism which the \u2018Good doctor\u2019 finds deeply offensive.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, if he ever perceived the true nature of the Voerman Sisters he\u2019d probably have locked them up for intensive study (No euphemism here, he\u2019d find their condition an absolutely fascinating case to study): otherwise I suspect he\u2019s prefer the organised psychopath over the disorganised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T10:03:09-08:00","id":1548619,"title":"","content":"One more thing - it occurred to me while contemplating a possible history for \u2018Damsel\u2019 that one could very easily make her an older version of Ariane (nee Jane) a Brujah embraced by a Chicago Anarch who liked the cut of her jib and set off in search of pastures anew after the War of Chicago.<br /> <br /> From what information I can access online there\u2019s nothing that directly contradicts this identification (and it would be not inappropriate to make one of the BLOODLINES characters somebody embraced in AD 1992 - assuming that \u2018Nines\u2019 Rodriguez picked up some useful tips on how to survive a Werewolf attack from somebody who presumably dodged her fair share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T10:14:07-08:00","id":1548620,"title":"","content":"I feel that Booth's gang should include someone who is clearly a homage to Spicoli from Fast Times at Ridgemont High, as well as a mash up of Alex Winter's characters from The Lost Boys and Bill &amp; Ted (and maybe even a nod to Death Wish 3), and a slightly clueless undercover FBI agent who fell under Booth's influence (giving a perfect excuse to get FBI-SAD entangled in all this). Perhaps also something similar to Courtney Thorne-Smith's character in 1987's Summer School, a young surfer who became infatuated with Booth as an older mentor type and ended up a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T17:46:28-08:00","id":1548638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548620#post1548620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that Booth's gang should include someone who is clearly a homage to Spicoli from Fast Times at Ridgemont High, as well as a mash up of Alex Winter's characters from The Lost Boys and Bill &amp; Ted (and maybe even a nod to Death Wish 3), and a slightly clueless undercover FBI agent who fell under Booth's influence (giving a perfect excuse to get FBI-SAD entangled in all this). Perhaps also something similar to Courtney Thorne-Smith's character in 1987's Summer School, a young surfer who became infatuated with Booth as an older mentor type and ended up a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, back in the '90's, I got all my NPC ideas from characters from movies. I tried not to make it so obvious and use ones from movies we watched a lot like Lost Boys and the Crow. I used movies I've seen (because, that's all there was to do back then), that my friends may not have seen like The Cutting Edge and Career Opportunities; None of my RPG friends saw True Romance or Judgement Night. However, when I used Rice's Druid Grove, I got called out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T18:06:38-08:00","id":1548643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548638#post1548638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, back in the '90's, I got all my NPC ideas from characters from movies. I tried not to make it so obvious and use ones from movies we watched a lot like Lost Boys and the Crow. I used movies I've seen (because, that's all there was to do back then), that my friends may not have seen like The Cutting Edge and Career Opportunities; None of my RPG friends saw True Romance or Judgement Night. However, when I used Rice's Druid Grove, I got called out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once got away with a Sheriff who was just Brigitte Nielsen's character from Beverly Hills Cop 2 as a Brujah. I am kind of disappointed no one noticed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T22:20:34-08:00","id":1548653,"title":"","content":"In LABN, Steve Booth's gang of vampire surfers is a very real thing. I'm just not using it in my chronicle. Booth will still be there with a small band of bro vampire surfers, but they're not some gang of warlord surfers, and I'm moving them from Long Beach to Santa Monica Bay. They'll be &quot;slacker&quot; vampires who pretty much just want to feed on drunk party goers and party on, and not really care about politics.<br /> <br /> I don't intend them to be jokes because they're all physically fit and mostly Brujah, and Booth could be disruptive if he started caring about politics or if he felt his pals were being muscled out. However, I want them as a counterweight to the heavy politics a lot of other NPCs will be doing. I just have much more interesting factions I'd rather use as &quot;gangs&quot; or baronies.<br /> <br /> Booth and his buds wander up and down the beach from Malibu to Palos Verde, and they even have a party boat they sometimes take down to Santa Catalina Island. They're harmless enough (and actually responsible in their feedings) that the barons of those area - Fortier, MacNeil, and even Geduld - tolerate them. They actually have a decent size herd of blood bonded mortal surfers that party with them, so they're mostly self sufficient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548620#post1548620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps also something similar to Courtney Thorne-Smith's character in 1987's Summer School, a young surfer who became infatuated with Booth as an older mentor type and ended up a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah! I'm definitely using that character as one of Booth's fellow surfers. I may also use some Point Break characters as inspiration as well. Good ideas. I may keep them to around 3 male and 3 female vampires as the core group with several hangers on that party with them now and again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T22:32:05-08:00","id":1548654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548601#post1548601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ncidentally, \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 is not meant to be a \u2018Fish Malk\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, I am not as intrigued by the good count as you are. It is very likely Count Rigatoni perished sometime after Bela's embrace in the chaos of Sabbat attacks and the general violence of the Free States. Obviously, a tragedy. Some of the older vampires in LA may still remember him and the amusement he provided before going into the dialogue of &quot;I wonder whatever happened to him.&quot;<br /> <br /> LABN said there were various &quot;counts&quot; who liked to cosplay as Dracula (mostly Malks, but not all of them) and Count Rigatoni was simply one of them. While not possibly Fish Malks, they were clearly in the vein of Malkavians being used as amusing gimmicks instead of actual characters. I like my Malkavians to have a little more substance to them. Plus once you have Bela, you don't need anyone else like him.<br /> <br /> But everyone has different tastes so everyone is going to design their chronicle differently. Even if it is something I won't be using, somebody else will do something fun with it in their own chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T23:01:26-08:00","id":1548656,"title":"","content":"One thing I need to do is decide how to portray the Sons of the Crypt. We're actually given very little information about them despite them being an important element in the setting. I'll be making a distinction between the vampire &quot;gang&quot; and the actual mortal gang they control because I just can't bring myself to use the same name for both. Your mileage may vary.<br /> <br /> I don't want to get too much into its leader also being a secret member of the Sabbat. I will eventually post a separate thread on the Sabbat in LA. However, some of that will be addressed here.<br /> <br /> I don't see the entire gang (LABN gives them 25 members, making them the largest gang/coterie) being Sabbat. That many would probably be exposed. But I expect there is a small core group of Sabbat (likely only Mohammed's childer, but possibly one or two recruits) inside the gang who comprise its leadership. I'm not sure what a good number of actual Sabbat inside the Crypts would be.<br /> <br /> I imagine Mohammed teamed up with some surviving anarch Brujah to form the original vampire gang, and they were the original leadership. Most of them have &quot;unfortunately&quot; perished in their efforts at expanding territory, so Mohammed is the only surviving original member. To him, most of the Crypt's Sons will need to be destroyed once the Sabbat launch their next crusade. They are just disposable cannon fodder he uses to take out the anarch leadership. However, I imagine when the Sabbat do attack and the initial war bands assemble, he will offer some of the Sons the opportunity to join with the Sabbat and perform the vaulderie.<br /> <br /> I imagine Mohammed poses as a Brujah. And I might even change his clan from Lasombra to Brujah anti-tribu. (To change things up, I may even have a vampire in some other &quot;gang&quot; have the Flaw where they do not cast reflections to make PCs think this other person must be Lasombra and therefore Sabbat). <br /> <br /> Should every member of the Sons be recruited from the Crips (or one of their allied gangs)? That would limit them as a &quot;gang&quot;, but maybe that's OK. There are certainly other vampires they might make use of, but given their extreme territoriality, I'd doubt they'd allow even allies/friends to feed. I think keeping a very strong &quot;us versus them&quot; attitude is essential for Mohammed to use them as a weapon against the other anarchs. So he might allow some exchange of boons or favors, but nothing like allowing them to feed on a regular basis. Only if they go full-in and join the Sons of the Crypts and accept Mohammed's absolute leadership would he allow them to feed. I think an all or nothing attitude is essential.<br /> <br /> I suspect every member of the gang is Brujah vampire native to that part of the city (mostly black, but a few may be other ethnicities from ethnic gangs allied to the Crips). I'll be watching The Wire and stealing a lot of characters from that show to transplant them from Baltimore to LA just so I can have some real characters instead of goons without personality. For these neonates, a lot of their culture and loyalty is to Mohammed as one of their own, and wanting one of their own to be the real ruler of LA, not some Scotsman who's actually an elder in vampire terms.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'll also have plenty of other black vampires not affiliated with the Sons. Mostly in the Barony of Angels, but also scattered in others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T04:51:18-08:00","id":1548667,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019d suggest mining crime dramas specifically set in LA (or at least somewhere in Southern California) rather than importing characters all the way from Maryland to the West Coast - unless part of the character\u2019s background is time in Baltimore - given that gang culture is intensely local and that there\u2019s a whole continent between THE WIRE and the City of Angels.<br /> <br /> I also like your idea of the Crypts being a gang within a gang (or possibly several gangs: it would make sense if \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 made sure to pull his recruits from just about every gang with a suitable composition - I.e. African American ancestry), with Mohammed\u2019s own brood representing yet another level of secrecy.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if you\u2019re going with that sort of layers within layers approach, I\u2019d argue that keeping Mohammed of the Crypts as a Lasombra makes more sense - since allowing player characters the option to expose him as a Lasombra, rather than a Brujah would give them a chance to achieve a significant victory against the character without removing him as an ongoing threat (Heck, \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 publicly declaring himself Lasombra <i>antitribu</i> would be an interesting exercise in spin control that would highlight his ingenuity and resilience, while still having a dramatic impact on his own political situation and that of Los Angeles).<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, it might be interesting to lean into the \u2018half Anarch, half Sabbat\u2019 nature of Mohammed of the Crypts when describing Sabbat activities within the Free States - I\u2019d bet cash money that there are elements within the sect who question whether \u2018Papa Crypt\u2019 and his Sons represent their Fifth Column within the Free States or just a private fiefdom for an individual playing both sides (This interpretation would be especially apt if you run with the idea that the Crypts pull recruits from just about every African American street gang, sooner or later.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, I\u2019ve been assuming that while Mohammed was Embraced ahead of the Big Sabbat Push in the 1960s he wasn\u2019t part of a mass embrace: whomsoever \u2018Tarantine\u2019* may have been, he would seem to have picked the future al-Muthlim for his brains, not a meat-shield.<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>Incidentally, while the name might well have been picked by the author as an homage to Quentin Tarantino, the name itself suggests a connection to the Tarantine cavalry of Ancient Italy (Back in the days when it was \u2018Magna Graecia\u2019) suggesting either that Mohammed the Crypt\u2019s sire was very, very old or (More probably) that he\u2019d diablerised a very opd<br /> vampire and taken their name as a trophy.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T05:51:44-08:00","id":1548668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548620#post1548620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that Booth's gang should include someone who is clearly a homage to Spicoli from Fast Times at Ridgemont High, as well as a mash up of Alex Winter's characters from The Lost Boys and Bill &amp; Ted (and maybe even a nod to Death Wish 3), and a slightly clueless undercover FBI agent who fell under Booth's influence (giving a perfect excuse to get FBI-SAD entangled in all this). Perhaps also something similar to Courtney Thorne-Smith's character in 1987's Summer School, a young surfer who became infatuated with Booth as an older mentor type and ended up a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d suggest throw in some homages to the BEACH PRTY movies and the GIDGET franchise (novels, films, TV) at least in terms of names and faces for the coterie - particularly the latter, since it was based on descriptions by the author\u2019s daughter (namesake of the title character) of California surf culture from a time and place with which Steve Booth would have been quite familiar (Heck, since he was born in AD 1942 he would have been only a year younger than Kathy \u2018Gidget\u2019 Kohner and may well have been part of the youth crowd she surfed with in the Malibu area).<br /> <br /> Given that Steve Booth seems to have been a night surfer even before he became a vampire, he might even have been one of the inspirations for \u2018Moondoggie\u2019 (The fictional Gidget\u2019s love interest from the novels and at least some of the adaptions) - incidentally, that nickname was apparently based on the character\u2019s fondness for surfing at night and I can absolutely imagine Steve Booth wearing it with pride.<br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming that Steve is \u2018Moondoggie\u2019, one assumes that his coterie would include a \u2018Big Kahuna\u2019 (One imagines this as a native Hawaiian who\u2019s been surfing longer than any of them, but tends to be a little less deep in the \u2018Surf dude\u2019 mindset than the rest because, well, he predates it - perhaps make him a young US Navy veteran who got made in the Los Angeles area at the time of WWII?); a \u2018Sandy\u2019 (A nod to Sandra Dee, the first actress to play GIDGET on live action) and/or an \u2018Angel\u2019 (Go ahead, just guess how a vampire from Los Angeles got the name) and possibly a \u2018Professor\u2019 (\u2018Prof\u2019?), as a nod to the fictional Gidget\u2019s dear old dad.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if Prof is the youngest and dumbest of the lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I recently learned that Mark Twain himself, on a visit to Hawai\u2019i actually tried his hand at \u2018surf-bathing\u2019 and, in his inimitable style, describes how \u201cNone but natives ever master the art of surf-bathing thoroughly\u201d (Apparently he got the right board, the right wave and the right instructions, but lacked the right reflexes): coupled with an awareness that San Diego was something of a surfing hot-spot, this gave me the delightful mental image for a character whom I share with you now.<br /> <br /> <br /> GEORGE HANNIBAL GRIFFIN<br /> <br /> - Almost universally know as \u2018Huck\u2019 (or, if we\u2019re feeling formal, \u2018Huckleberry\u2019), the character in question is on of Tara Kearney\u2019s brood who started in Mississippi in the 1830s (Spent some time as a printer\u2019s boy, as a hand on a Mississippi River boat etc) before heading west sometime in the mid to late 1850s, where he met and was Embraced by Tara Kearney because he had a way with words that she believed would be useful (and which she may even have found delightful, although it\u2019s always hard to tell with that \u2018Mother knows best\u2019 poker face).<br /> <br /> - Not entirely delighted by this situation, but willing to \u2018live\u2019 with it, Huck seized the opportunity offered by the scattering of Tara\u2019s brood into the War Between the States to get out from under her thumb and head further West (Though evidence suggests he kept up better relations than most with the Boss Lady by sending her letters concerning his own movements and on behalf of those brood-mates he ran into \u2026 especially after the War started going quite badly for some of them).<br /> <br /> Asked whether he fought for the North or the South, Huck would always reply \u201cGood question. I got shot in the head, so we\u2019ll have to ask someone else\u201d (\u201cGot shot in the head\u201d remains his favourite excuse and a recurring punchline).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Reaching the Pacific Coast at some point after the American Civil War, he\u2019s known to have spent time in San Francisco and to have visited Hawai\u2019i at some point (Whether he actually took a shot at \u2018surf-bathing\u2019 while there remains lost to the ages, but he might well have been able to observe the practice, at least).<br /> <br /> He\u2019s very proud to boast a number of Mark Twain stories (The two were from the same part of the world originally, though they took different courses thereafter, and still seem to share a sense of humour), some of which might even be true, but claims that it was he who originally told the famous frog story that the former Samuel Clemens used to make his name in the world of literature remain extremely doubtful.<br /> <br /> <br /> - While a fair amount of his career remains unrecorded (He kept sending letter to Tara in Dallas, but he probably didn\u2019t tell her everything and she hasn\u2019t exactly shared her correspondence) we do know that he also kept in touch with the scattered El Paso brood and wound up in San Diego, California, at some point after the rail link went in.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s thought to have acted as the Brujah primogen under Prince Maria (and may well have been one of the key elements allowing her to assert praxis and survive in the first place), with the job becoming much less of a sinecure after the massive influxes of \u2018Prohibition tourists\u2019 during the 1920s.<br /> <br /> What role he played in the assassination of the first Prince of San Diego remains obscure, but he was most certainly passing actionable intelligence to Tara Kearney and posse\u2019d up with the text of her brood during the Second Anarch Revolt and played a key role in Tara assuming control over San Diego (At least in the early days).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Somewhat marginalised as Tara solidified her control over San Diego (\u2018Mother knows best\u2019 is an attitude easier to smile at from half a continent away and Huck is an Anarch by conviction, albeit somewhat casual conviction, rather than convenience) he found himself gravitating to the distraction and sense of freedom offered by the burgeoning surf culture.<br /> <br /> As a result, he found himself pulled into the social circles of Steve Booth and perhaps the unlikeliest member of \u2018The Surf Baron\u2019s\u2019 extensive network of friends (Often as a friendly rival to the LA surf set, particularly as \u201cTheir man in Tara Country\u201d).<br /> <br /> Rumours that he and Marguerite are working to shape Steve into an actual Baron (or at the very least seeking to turn his long list of friends into an actual network) remain unconfirmed.<br /> <br /> <br /> AUTHOR\u2019S NOTE: Yes, this is a shameless effort to create a character best summed up as \u201cWhat if Samuel Clemens became a vampire, not Mark Twain?\u201d (Or, more succinctly as \u2018Mark Twain, Surfer dude\u2019), but that mental image was played by a young Woody Harrelson in a moustache and I couldn\u2019t resist it.<br /> <br /> Also, for my money Tara Kearney had to have some sort of informant inside San Diego even before the Second Anarch Revolt (Arriving in California from Texas and somehow finding exactly the right city to make her very, very own domain right after the local Prince was retired, presumably with Extreme Prejudice, isn\u2019t just a stroke of luck: either Tara Kearney had her very own magic lamp or she had an agent in the future Free States).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T06:07:19-08:00","id":1548669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548620#post1548620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that Booth's gang should include someone who is clearly a homage to Spicoli from Fast Times at Ridgemont High, as well as a mash up of Alex Winter's characters from The Lost Boys and Bill &amp; Ted (and maybe even a nod to Death Wish 3), and a slightly clueless undercover FBI agent who fell under Booth's influence (giving a perfect excuse to get FBI-SAD entangled in all this). Perhaps also something similar to Courtney Thorne-Smith's character in 1987's Summer School, a young surfer who became infatuated with Booth as an older mentor type and ended up a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d suggest throw in some homages to the BEACH PRTY movies and the GIDGET franchise (novels, films, TV) at least in terms of names and faces for the coterie - particularly the latter, since it was based on descriptions by the author\u2019s daughter (namesake of the title character) of California surf culture from a time and place with which Steve Booth would have been quite familiar (Heck, since he was born in AD 1942 he would have been only a year younger than Kathy \u2018Gidget\u2019 Kohner and may well have been part of the youth crowd she surfed with in the Malibu area).<br /> <br /> Given that Steve Booth seems to have been a night surfer even before he became a vampire, he might even have been one of the inspirations for \u2018Moondoggie\u2019 (The fictional Gidget\u2019s love interest from the novels and at least some of the adaptions) - incidentally, that nickname was apparently based on the character\u2019s fondness for surfing at night and I can absolutely imagine Steve Booth wearing it with pride.<br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming that Steve is \u2018Moondoggie\u2019, one assumes that his coterie would include a \u2018Big Kahuna\u2019 (One imagines this as a native Hawaiian who\u2019s been surfing longer than any of them, but tends to be a little less deep in the \u2018Surf dude\u2019 mindset than the rest because, well, he predates it - perhaps make him a young US Navy veteran who got made in the Los Angeles area at the time of WWII?); a \u2018Sandy\u2019 (A nod to Sandra Dee, the first actress to play GIDGET on live action) and/or an \u2018Angel\u2019 (Go ahead, just guess how a vampire from Los Angeles got the name) and possibly a \u2018Professor\u2019 (\u2018Prof\u2019?), as a nod to the fictional Gidget\u2019s dear old dad.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if Prof is the youngest and dumbest of the lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I recently learned that Mark Twain himself, on a visit to Hawai\u2019i actually tried his hand at \u2018surf-bathing\u2019 and, in his inimitable style, describes how \