ally took a shot at \u2018surf-bathing\u2019 while there remains lost to the ages, but he might well have been able to observe the practice, at least).<br /> <br /> He\u2019s very proud to boast a number of Mark Twain stories (The two were from the same part of the world originally, though they took different courses thereafter, and still seem to share a sense of humour), some of which might even be true, but claims that it was he who originally told the famous frog story that the former Samuel Clemens used to make his name in the world of literature remain extremely doubtful.<br /> <br /> <br /> - While a fair amount of his career remains unrecorded (He kept sending letter to Tara in Dallas, but he probably didn\u2019t tell her everything and she hasn\u2019t exactly shared her correspondence) we do know that he also kept in touch with the scattered El Paso brood and wound up in San Diego, California, at some point after the rail link went in.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s thought to have acted as the Brujah primogen under Prince Maria (and may well have been one of the key elements allowing her to assert praxis and survive in the first place), with the job becoming much less of a sinecure after the massive influxes of \u2018Prohibition tourists\u2019 during the 1920s.<br /> <br /> What role he played in the assassination of the first Prince of San Diego remains obscure, but he was most certainly passing actionable intelligence to Tara Kearney and posse\u2019d up with the text of her brood during the Second Anarch Revolt and played a key role in Tara assuming control over San Diego (At least in the early days).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Somewhat marginalised as Tara solidified her control over San Diego (\u2018Mother knows best\u2019 is an attitude easier to smile at from half a continent away and Huck is an Anarch by conviction, albeit somewhat casual conviction, rather than convenience) he found himself gravitating to the distraction and sense of freedom offered by the burgeoning surf culture.<br /> <br /> As a result, he found himself pulled into the social circles of Steve Booth and perhaps the unlikeliest member of \u2018The Surf Baron\u2019s\u2019 extensive network of friends (Often as a friendly rival to the LA surf set, particularly as \u201cTheir man in Tara Country\u201d).<br /> <br /> Rumours that he and Marguerite are working to shape Steve into an actual Baron (or at the very least seeking to turn his long list of friends into an actual network) remain unconfirmed.<br /> <br /> <br /> AUTHOR\u2019S NOTE: Yes, this is a shameless effort to create a character best summed up as \u201cWhat if Samuel Clemens became a vampire, not Mark Twain?\u201d (Or, more succinctly as \u2018Mark Twain, Surfer dude\u2019), but that mental image was played by a young Woody Harrelson in a moustache and I couldn\u2019t resist it.<br /> <br /> Also, for my money Tara Kearney had to have some sort of informant inside San Diego even before the Second Anarch Revolt (Arriving in California from Texas and somehow finding exactly the right city to make her very, very own domain right after the local Prince was retired, presumably with Extreme Prejudice, isn\u2019t just a stroke of luck: either Tara Kearney had her very own magic lamp or she had an agent in the future Free States).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T06:07:19-08:00","id":1548670,"title":"","content":"Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I quite understand that not everyone will share my fondness for the notion of a \u2018Count Rigatoni\u2019 and would certainly not insist on his continuing presence as of the LA ecosystem (My notion was that the character could, in fact, be played as a sort of \u2018Bela\u2019 who could be deployed in cities other than Los Angeles to serve as the same sort of tongue in cheek rebuke to the sort of Vampire Expert who starts their speeches with \u201cThis isn\u2019t the movies!\u201d despite being part of a big budget Hollywood production*).<br /> <br /> If nothing else, should you want to get rid of the character you could simply suggest that, after years in the Anarch Free States (Legend has it that he dipped into Sabbat country at one point - or at least into Tijuana, the exact status of which remains sharply disputed - but nobody sensible could possibly believe that), Count Rigatoni tried out his act in a Camarilla city and suffered accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>Also that an individual who reflected the twists and turns through which various depictions of Count Dracula have taken the character across the decades whilst \u2018Bela\u2019 himself remains THE Classic Hollywood Dracula might be an amusing occasional foil to the character (Especially if played by the likes of Mr Peter MacNicol or Mr Mark Hamill - the latter of whom remains my pick to play the Holo-Dracula depicted in a LOWER DECKS comic book storyline.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T06:08:13-08:00","id":1548671,"title":"","content":"Eh?!? The website seems to have duplicated at least one of my posts for some reason \u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T12:37:46-08:00","id":1548683,"title":"","content":"I haven\u2019t quite worked out \u2018Blood Types\u2019 for all the canon Ventrue NPCs, but I <i>did</i> want to share those that have occurred to me and my basic rules for coming up with individual manifestations of the \u2018Blue Bloods\u2019 Clan Curse in PCs &amp; NPCs:-<br /> <br /> - \u2018Blood Types\u2019 should be specific, but archetypical rather than generic (To my mind \u2018Rough trade\u2019 would be acceptable, \u2018Males\u2019 would not)<br /> <br /> <i>Archetypes, after all, allow us an intuitive understanding of what appeals to the character without requiring excessive explanation (Although further explanation might give us a deeper understanding not only of what appealed to the character in the first place, but what continues to hold their interest, for good and ill)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> - The \u2018Blood Type\u2019 should have been readily available during the character\u2019s earliest nights as a Vampire, but not too ubiquitous (Familiarity breeds contempt, after all): it<br /> may have become more or less common in the years, decades/centuries/millennia since, though<br /> <br /> <i>This rule applies more to elders than to fledgelings, but it\u2019s common sense that a vampire isn\u2019t going to starve themselves (Though the more adventurous might well fixate on a Type that involves a certain degree of risk - for example a vampire who was a Renaissance monk might well chase \u2018Naughty nuns\u2019)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> - The vampire\u2019s choice of \u2018Blood Type\u2019 should never seem entirely-innocuous, The choice should provide an insight into what gets a Ventrue\u2019s motor running, ideally for better <i><b>and</b></i> for worse<br /> <br /> <i>To my mind the entire point of the Ventrue clan curse is not merely to make them look snooty: like learning a public figure\u2019s sexual preferences, it punctures the aura of majesty and pragmatic mastery with which the Clan of Kings surrounds itself - it is, after all, a Curse</i><br /> <br /> <br /> One last, much less essential point, is that the perfect choice of Blood Type should have a \u2018Good\u2019, a \u2018Bad\u2019 and an \u2018Ugly\u2019 reason for the vampire to have been drawn to it -<br /> <br /> - For Example:<br /> <br /> JESUS RAMIREZ (\u2018Blood Type\u2019 Bully Boys)<br /> <br /> The Good - Being the unwilling servant of a cruel master, Ramirez making a habit of drinking from the muscle meant that sometimes the boss had to repress the peasants with thugs not operating at their peak (Much to his master\u2019s annoyance)<br /> <br /> <br /> The Bad - Jesus Ramirez isn\u2019t exactly a Herculean figure and there\u2019s at least some evidence he targets big, burly thug-types to soothe old grudges against those better built than himself<br /> <br /> <br /> The Ugly - as a former enforcer himself, Jesus Ramirez could be guaranteed a steady supply of muscle-headed bullies whether he munched his own master\u2019s myrmidons or the Boss started a rumble with the opposition purely to keep his henchman in vitae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":". 02-21-2025, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T17:38:23-08:00","id":1548740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548610#post1548610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially if their leader is some sort of charismatic guru in the vein of Patrick Swayze in Point Break crossed with Keiffer Sutherland in The Lost Boys.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a very long time since I watched Point Break, but I was willing to watch it on YouTube as I was going to bed. I completely forgot about the whole philosophy of life espoused by Patrick Swayze's character (and TBH almost the entirety of the movie). <br /> <br /> However, now that I am thinking about that whole zen-surfer attitude, I think there's a lot I can apply to Booth. I also think it might be an interesting way to have a character who's interested in Golconda. Booth and his buddies like being vampires. They like the idea of being perpetually young and the powers it provides. They just don't like the negatives. So they'll have an interesting approach to Golconda as opposed to the more traditional morality inclined version of most Golconda seekers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-23T17:45:28-08:00","id":1548741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548683#post1548683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2018Blood Types\u2019 should be specific, but archetypical rather than generic (To my mind \u2018Rough trade\u2019 would be acceptable, \u2018Males\u2019 would not)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that such an approach tends to make for stronger characters, but I think it's good that Ventrue can range all over the place in terms of their feeding restrictions. The corebook gives some very lenient feeding restrictions (like &quot;not animals&quot;), and we have examples of characters only able to feed on one person (although that is not plausible at all and requires some changes). And I think it can be good for a game to have Ventrue characters who vary wildly on the extent and ease as to their restriction. It makes for more varied characters, and interesting dynamics within the clan. Are certain Ventrue jealous that one member has very generous &quot;limitations&quot;? Or perhaps they look down upon her for not having rarefied tastes?<br /> <br /> But as a general guideline, I don't think there's anything wrong with your approach, and I usually do something like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T11:55:28-08:00","id":1548768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548740#post1548740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's been a very long time since I watched Point Break, but I was willing to watch it on YouTube as I was going to bed. I completely forgot about the whole philosophy of life espoused by Patrick Swayze's character (and TBH almost the entirety of the movie).<br /> <br /> However, now that I am thinking about that whole zen-surfer attitude, I think there's a lot I can apply to Booth. I also think it might be an interesting way to have a character who's interested in Golconda. Booth and his buddies like being vampires. They like the idea of being perpetually young and the powers it provides. They just don't like the negatives. So they'll have an interesting approach to Golconda as opposed to the more traditional morality inclined version of most Golconda seekers.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, there needs to be at least one setting out there with Keanu Reeves as a Surfer Dude Vampire, so why not make it this one, brah?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> , your point about Ventrue \u2018blood types\u2019 is well-taken (Though for my money the one-person feeding restriction makes sense on a storytelling level, if nothing else - what better epitome of a tragically, romantically, creepily strong bond suitable for Gothic Romance and Tragedy than a vampire being literally unable to live without someone?).<br /> <br /> I admit to preferring more specific than generic feeding restrictions because they help make sense of the Clan Ventrue tendency to wind up in charge: when the very nature of your bloodline curse requires you to make very specific arrangements or perish (Whether through starvation or being caught up or caught out in diablerie), it makes sense that a lineage of vampires would develop considerable organisational competence and a vested interest in arranging the world to suit themselves (Not to mention in defending one\u2019s ability to do so).<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of Clan Ventrue, I wanted to discuss your suggestion in the \u2018Anarch domains\u2019 thread that Sebastian LaCroix be a Childe of Baron Fortier: it\u2019s an interesting idea and it certainly gives him a strong stake in Los Angeles, though it does beg the question of where Louis Fortier is during the events of the game, in a scenario where his own progeny is an embarrassment to the whole bloodline (On the other hand it\u2019s interesting to wonder if one of his \u2018Brides\u2019 would make a logical choice for the sire of a Ventrue PC, if their \u2018Blood Daddy\u2019 were out of the picture and their brood-mate were turning into an Idiot Fail Childe).<br /> <br /> Anyway, my preference would be to show LaCroix as a Camarilla agent crafty enough to approach Baron Fortier with an offer of \u2018fictive kinship\u2019 - that is, offering Fortier recognition as the member of a prestigious Old World bloodline in return for the Baron arranging some discrete introductions and the occasional back-scratch.<br /> <br /> <br /> While this may sound like small change to some, it\u2019s worth considering that Louis Fortier was an aristocrat in life who has absolutely no idea whether the vampire who embraced him was the stuff of legend or a Clan embarrassment - being able to \u2018reconnect\u2019 with an extremely prestigious bloodline would undoubtedly be worth serious political capital in Ventrue political circles (On top old the fact that having a slightly less hostile back-channel of communications open to the Camarilla might offer it\u2019s own benefits).<br /> <br /> That this \u2018fictive kinship\u2019 would be of immense value to a Camarilla agent, but something of a liability to a Prince of Los Angeles (Adding Fortier\u2019s widespread unpopularity to the inherent hostility to a Camarilla prince imposing themselves on a former Anarch domain) is a feature, rather than a bug.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the record, my characterisation of Prince Sebastian LaCroix would be as an immensely competent agent of the Camarilla promoted past his competence as a \u2018parachute Prince\u2019 in LA, most likely due to a crafty rival reasoning that no matter how much of a poison chalice Los Angeles might be, it was too juicy a prize for a seriously ambitious Kindred to pass on (Especially if the offer were made by Elders of the Ivory Tower, persuaded that it was better - at least for them - to risk an expendable agent than to risk the creation of a powerful rival by promoting some local hero or handing the crown jewel of California to a Kindred with the demonstrated ability to make a great city their own).<br /> <br /> Hence LA winding up with a Ventrue prince who was in over his head, a true successor to Don Sebastian (Whom I tend to imagine as very capable of dominating a small town or even a regional hub, but increasingly out of his depth as Los Angeles grew into a World City).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T12:27:27-08:00","id":1548769,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019m planning to post my ideas for Maria, the late Prince of San Diego, tomorrow - I have a number of possible concepts, otherwise I might have posted something more tonight - but may I also ask if there are any characters you would specifically like/prefer to discuss? <br /> <br /> (Incidentally, I\u2019m also looking over <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a>\u2019s old archetypes thread - trying to work out which would make the most interesting picks for the Free States - I noted that \u2018The Stuntman\u2019 has an explicit connection to Hollywood, but for my money \u2018The Elder Representative\u2019 might be a more interesting pick than (for example) \u2018The Anarch Terrorist\u2019, since it make sense that Brujah elders elsewhere would want an eye on the latest utopian effort (and, unlike a number of the other Brujah archetypes, this one isn\u2019t covered by canon NPCs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-25T17:37:03-08:00","id":1548772,"title":"","content":"There are a bunch of early ones you can easily throw together as a semi-generic Anarch gang. The Brujah terr\u00f6rist or rapper, the Gangrel urban commando, and the Malkavian reality buster or conspiracy theorist, as a start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-27T06:54:11-08:00","id":1548804,"title":"","content":"Very true - I\u2019m trying to specifically pick out those with canon ties to LA and southern CA (At this point I only have the Stuntman, the Plastic Surgeon and the Speed Metal Guitarist, as I\u2019m working through your thread a piece at a time).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also trying to pick out archetypes that work as NPCs, rather PC types - especially ones that are a little bit left field, to help keep things interesting.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll keep plugging away and we\u2019ll see what comes of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-27T08:01:07-08:00","id":1548805,"title":"","content":"Something related to a specific LA BY NIGHT character that I only realised today is that Don Armando de Madrid (Sire of Alonso Guillen of Clan Nosferatu) becomes much more interesting when one learns that Madrid is one of the key Sabbat outposts in Europe.<br /> <br /> Assuming that Don Armando <i>does</i> hail from Madrid itself, rather than using that name as an alias, it\u2019s<br /> possible that he is (or was) a Nosferatu antitribu - whether aligned with the Sabbat, more of an Anarch or simply Autarkis.<br /> <br /> In any case it\u2019s perfectly possible that Alonso Guillen was brought up outside Camarilla society - and may have sought out his sister in California seeking to escape a vampiric environment less than conducive to maintaining a solid Humanity rating (Or which scared the young fellow spitless).<br /> <br /> Admittedly with tragic results, but that\u2019s the sort of risk you run when you\u2019re THE Most Classically Gothic Vampire in the LA basin.<br /> <br /> <br /> Think about it: Alonso Guillen is the disfigured son of a Spanish aristocratic family with a beautiful younger sister who made her life a very long way off from little brother (I\u2019m assuming that a key part of the reason a purportedly successful lady of the Spanish court wound up in a provincial backwater on the other side of the world is that her brother\u2019s deformities were at least whispered, if not common knowledge, making it easier to make a decently prestigious match as a \u2018mail order bride\u2019); was so badly-deformed that a Nosferatu (Probably one of noble ancestry, given the title \u2018Don Armando\u2019, possibly even one embracing a distant relation) decided that becoming a vampire would improve his condition; nonetheless found himself in an underworld which so disturbed him that he deliberately sought out his presumably-beloved (or at least much-admired) sister - from which one May deduce that his parents were either dead or living a little too close to his Sire\u2019s base of operations; and, descending on his last living relative seeking some human comfort was refused, called a monster, and nonetheless sought to make his sister as he was (Possibly hoping this change of perspective would help forge a closer connection between them); Failing quite spectacularly and killing the only witness (His brother in law) he hares off into the wilderness and lives the life of a wandering spirit (Though apparently one with a continuing desire to receive and bestow kindnesses \u2026 apparently tempered by a refusal to acknowledge this kindness and desperation for kindness, given \u2018Nature: Caregiver/Demeanour: Curmudgeon\u2019).<br /> <br /> Honestly, this really is the stuff of classic Gothic fiction - complete with all the tragedy of a hideous monster desperate for love and lashing out when he does not (and possibly cannot hope to) receive it - and I\u2019m more than a little fascinated by the character as a result.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t hurt that he seems to be second only to Christopher* in length of years spent as a vampire in LA (and, while solitary by habit, far more likely to accept and benefit from gestures of friendship than the Peter Pan of Clan Toreador), which could make him a key source of information on local history (However incomplete, due to his outsider perspective and lack of fluency in any language but Spanish).<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>It\u2019s interesting to wonder how he managed to avoid the attentions of character who radiates \u2018Will kill the ugly for messing up the place and also for sport\u2019 energy: I wonder if Christopher was lazy and self-indulgent enough to have Don Sebastian (In the latter\u2019s days as a ghoul) on the trail of whomsoever murdered two prominent local residents and the Don took one look at that mess, made a half-hearted effort to do some tracking, then decided that discretion was the better part of valour (Possibly because Alonso\u2019s brother-in-law was a local rival whose loss was not resented) and then proceeded to stick with that policy even after he became a vampire himself (Partly due to reluctance to the difficulty involved with finding a Nosferatu who doesn\u2019t want to be found, partly due to the risk of running into local Lupines the further out into the wilderness one goes and not least due to his being kept busy with the work of a Prince with a growing brood &amp; growing city to handle).<br /> <br /> <br /> - </i>Getting intocharacterisation of Alonso himself, I tend to assume he\u2019s somebody mostly willing to live by himself but reluctant to completely sever his his to humanity - the sort of Nosferatu who keeps out of sight, feeding on those who are about to die (Animal &amp; human) but making a point of offering aid (Usually covert assistance) to those persons and those beasts who have been hurt, but stand a decent chance of recovering (I find it especially easy to imagine him treating injured animals and taking a close interest in following the comings &amp; goings of nocturnal creatures of the natural world - particularly flying creatures, with the inherent freedom from Earthly confines).<br /> <br /> He is, in other words, somebody who might well appear in the folklore of Spanish speaking California as an Angel of Death and a Guardian Angel (Possibly without the locals realising that these two are one and the same, much less one and the same with the hideous monster occasionally glimpsed when the sun is gone, but the deepest dusk has yet to settle).<br /> <br /> <br /> - I tend to imagine that, after the supremely horrible experience of that botched Embrace, he would be deeply reluctant to risk another such - further contributing to his fundamental loneliness: I find it easier to imagine the other Nosferatu of LA descending from agents sent out by his sire (or other elements in the Clan) to seek him out.<br /> <br /> Whether those agents actually managed to make a connection is an interesting question, given Alonso fled his own kind at least once; it also seems likely, as mentioned above, that Christopher and his brood would make existence in LA very, very difficult for Nosferatu during their heyday (Which would help explain why Alonso is the only Nosferatu specifically mentioned: I may have mentioned elsewhere that one also imagine LA as a town Gangrel have traditionally avoided, possibly due to some ugly history there but also quite possibly due to a dislike of the local Kindred culture).<br /> <br /> <br /> - It\u2019s interesting to note that he seems to have struck up an unlikely friendship with Henry Waters of the Vignes household (Clearly Henry lives up to that Humanity 7), but I\u2019ve also seen it noted that Alonso has ties to those two horrible sisters and seems amused by these old serial killers (Strongly hinting that while he\u2019s interested in keeping up human ties, he\u2019s either indifferent or desperate enough to fall in with the worst people in preference to going on alone: also that Humanity 5 may be the latest stage in his descent from an uncommonly sensitive Kindred to someone as monstrous in nature as he is in appearance).<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, after a somewhat disorganised ramble, my key suggestions are that any depiction of Alonso emphasise:<br /> <br /> (A) His longevity in LA - if he hasn\u2019t seen it all, he\u2019s seen more than most (and remembers it): he\u2019s also had time to make a major impression on LA folklore, as mentioned above, even if the stories don\u2019t have a perfectly clear idea of what and who he is.<br /> <br /> (B) His nature as a Classic Gothic Horror - all the tragedy, pathos and horror of his secret history &amp; solitary lifestyle (I\u2019m not sure what the best way to do this in writing would be, but in a visual adaptation I\u2019d suggest artists really lean into classic compositions, particularly those from the Silent Film NOSFERATU, setting up Alonso as an almost purely Gothic contestant to the prevailing Punk influence amongst the LA Kindred).<br /> <br /> (C) His appetite for kindnesses, both given and received, but also his painful vulnerability to the desperate desire to make some kind of human connection (With the associated risks of leaving him open to corruption by the wicked or triggering some horrifying spasm of rage if he feels slighted by some frightened innocent).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s easy to imagine an ongoing sub-plot of Alonso being carefully re-socialised by a party of PCs, assuming a willingness to take an interest in a potentially-dangerous stray on their part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-27T17:48:13-08:00","id":1548807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548769#post1548769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but may I also ask if there are any characters you would specifically like/prefer to discuss?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I am not impressed with the quality of the NPCs found in Los Angeles By Night. Most of the original ones (meaning the ones invented by this sourcebook, not characters already mentioned elsewhere) are uninteresting and mediocre. The Vignes family is somewhat interesting due to their family drama, but the characters involved take up way too much space for their pertinence to the setting.<br /> <br /> The only ones whom I think might be prove interesting are the four &quot;Brujah Idealists&quot; since they have a potential to be an interesting component to the setting. What exactly is it that they do? Who do they interact with? What impact may they have, even if indirectly?<br /> <br /> I'm more interested in the underdeveloped factions within the Free States. What other things can be done to make the Son's Crypts interesting? Who might also be members of La Hermandad, which in my imagination is less Mexican gangsters and more dedicated anarchists (as opposed to just anarchs). Lots of Hispanic gangsters or Kindred could be allied to La Hermandad, but La Hermandad itself is more interesting to me as some kind of anarchist secret society engaged in direct action. And of course, who else makes up the &quot;MacNeil Boys&quot;, the personal coterie of Jeremy MacNeil who police and control the Barony of Angels against the other gangs?<br /> <br /> While I think the LABN sourcebook overall is garbage, there are lots of good ideas in there that are underdeveloped and could have turned it into a great sourcebook. That's why I look upon LABN, other sources like the Bloodlines computer game, and others less as canon, and more as inspiration to steal from and develop on my own. My own tastes and perspective are probably less useful to those who want to approach things from a solely canon perspective.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T12:26:22-08:00","id":1548822,"title":"","content":"Having given a little thought to the \u2018MacNeil Boys\u2019, one tends to assume that it\u2019s core is what they used to call a chief\u2019s \u2019Fighting Tail\u2019 (The clansmen who followed him throughout a campaign, shielded him in battle and stuck around even after the fighting was over - not quite a military household or a staff, but more than just a fighting brotherhood) - presumably his close, personal friends like Crispus Attucks and other veterans of various adventures &amp; misadventures, including the coterie which helped to make the Second Anarch Revolt happen (and helped put down the Second Temple of Set*, as well as drive off the Sabbat in the 1960s).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also quite possible that the oldest and closest comrades of MacNeil act as an example to the admirers drawn to the most famous Anarch in LA from all over the city &amp; the world, as well as recruiters for the best of the local gangs - pulling the leading best &amp; brightest into his orbit long enough for the MacNeil to get to know them, befriend them, provide them with the sort of training that will help them hold leadership roles across the Free States and so forth (Not to mention grow MacNeil\u2019s own network and spread his philosophy)..<br /> <br /> <br /> *Incidentally, my mental image of the Nicholas who played a key role in making the \u2018Second Temple\u2019 possible, but also brought it tumbling down with his hostility to a rival priestess and curious decision to bring in MacNeil, is that he may well have been a Brujah convert to the Setite cause (Possibly even one with a personal connection to MacNeil), hence his survival even after the fall of the \u2018First Temple\u2019 and his willingness to risk bringing in LAs reigning Brujah hero (Also, the curious failure to bring in some senior Setites to straighten things out).<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming that the MacNeil Boys - probably a mix of MacNeil\u2019s own childer, his dearest friends, his most devoted admirers and the odd tourist - help make existence a little easier and more safe for their Chief to boot (Although MacNeil would likely emphasise a sense of fictive kinship and an even stronger sense of camaraderie over any sort of formal hierarchy).<br /> <br /> It seems quite possible that while this would be a Brujah-heavy group (Probably with members who go all the way back to the Old Country and the old wars, running from LA to the Midwest to Boston to Ireland and back to the Wars of the Three Kingdoms via the Civil War, the American Revolutionary War and the Jacobite Risings) but that MacNeil would make room for colleagues from other Clans - though I\u2019d bet that Toreador tend to be visitors, rather than part of the inner circle (Given MacNeil\u2019s ugly history with Don Sebastian and the high likelihood of an LA Toreador being of the late Prince\u2019s bloodline).<br /> <br /> Above all, I think we can safely say at least one or more of these fellows will be a bagpiper: MacNeil HATES \u2018Professional Scotsmen\u2019 with a mighty hatred, but he\u2019s too shrewd a warrior to deny himself the services of Scotland\u2019s greatest contribution to psychological warfare\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T23:26:15-08:00","id":1548866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548822#post1548822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having given a little thought to the \u2018MacNeil Boys\u2019, one tends to assume that it\u2019s core is what they used to call a chief\u2019s \u2019Fighting Tail\u2019 (The clansmen who followed him throughout a campaign, shielded him in battle and stuck around even after the fighting was over - not quite a military household or a staff, but more than just a fighting brotherhood) - presumably his close, personal friends like Crispus Attucks and other veterans of various adventures &amp; misadventures, including the coterie which helped to make the Second Anarch Revolt happen (and helped put down the Second Temple of Set*, as well as drive off the Sabbat in the 1960s).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not familiar with the term &quot;fighting tail&quot;, but I agree it is apt and MacNeil's expectation of his &quot;boys&quot; could very well meet that definition.<br /> <br /> I don't think he had such a group prior to the Free States. Despite his reputation as &quot;the Liberator&quot; afterwards, prior to 1944 he likely had more a reputation as a troublemaker than some radical revolutionary. While in the British Isles, his passion seemed more about the Scots and Irish rather than Kindred politics. And even after he arrived in North America, it's just said he was one of many Brujah &quot;forced westward&quot; by Ventrue expansion. Both Attucks and Foccart only seemed to arrive in LA after everything happened. So it's likely the MacNeil Boys were formed afterwards when MacNeil's reputation soared. As such, the Brujah (and possibly others) who joined him would have been whatever motley crew impressed him in the decades since. Most of them would likely be fairly recent neonates, but a few like Crispus might be Kindred he had befriended during his travels westward before he arrived in LA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548822#post1548822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, my mental image of the Nicholas who played a key role in making the \u2018Second Temple\u2019 possible, but also brought it tumbling down with his hostility to a rival priestess and curious decision to bring in MacNeil, is that he may well have been a Brujah convert to the Setite cause (Possibly even one with a personal connection to MacNeil), hence his survival even after the fall of the \u2018First Temple\u2019 and his willingness to risk bringing in LAs reigning Brujah hero (Also, the curious failure to bring in some senior Setites to straighten things out).</div> </div> </div> </div>You may have misread that section on Dawn Kavanaugh. Nicholas did not survive as the text clearly says he was killed in the attack. Nor did he inform MacNeil. He informed some other anarchs, and that his information reached MacNeil was not part of the plan. Likely he intended to destroy Dawn during the cover of the attack. However, there was an unnamed Brujah among MacNeil's coterie who had turned to the ways of Set and tipped off Dawn so she could escape. His current fate is not mentioned so it's up to the ST if he's still around. It sounds like you may be conflating these two different characters.<br /> <br /> I wish we had gotten a little more detail on the Setites. Dawn gets an extensive profile, but we're told very little of how she intends to proceed, or if there are existing Kindred waiting for her to return. We don't even know when the attack that destroyed the second temple took place (I assume sometime in the seventies). How the Setites should be used in the chronicle is something I intend its own thread on it, but there's no problem talking about individual Setites here.<br /> <br /> In any case, the ST has to make decision if that coterie member who tipped Dawn off is still around, and if so what he's like. This would have been an excellent character to include in the write ups than the various generic gang members for most of the clan. We can assume he's been &quot;corrupted&quot;, but how exactly? Is this just typical Hollywood excess? Feeding on vessels high on drugs? What exactly could be so scandalous that in an &quot;anything goes&quot; place like the Free States that the vampire needed to obtain it from the Setites? Or did Dawn just throw such great parties that certain Kindred just decided to join up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Gr63DiEUxw\" data-code=\"7Gr63DiEUxw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/7Gr63DiEUxw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T09:19:08-08:00","id":1548909,"title":"","content":"As I\u2019ve noted elsewhere, my sources are quite limited - at the moment mostly dependent on the White Wolf Wiki and an online review of the sourcebook LA BY NIGHT.<br /> <br /> All mistakes are, therefore, quite plainly my fault.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding your own points - <br /> <br /> (1) I agree with the notion that the MacNeil Boys almost certainly mustered in only after the Second Anarch Revolt, but it wouldn\u2019t surprise me if MacNeil (Whose career seems to have been adventurous for quite a long while) hadn\u2019t run with a coterie or three even prior to that point (If only during the inter-Kindred conflicts surrounding the Wars of the Three Kingdoms and the American Revolution), with the survivors of those previous posses presumably serving as the core of the much larger network now wearing MacNeil\u2019s name.<br /> <br /> N.B. One assumes that this would have occurred only after the Second Anarch Revolt made MacNeil not only storied but famous - with old acquaintances presumably rocking up to LA looking to take advantage of past association and old friends deciding to lend MacNeil their help.<br /> <br /> <br /> (2) One interesting question having over the exact membership of the MacNeil Boys is whether Jeremy MacNeil\u2019s past alignment with Clan Toreador - specifically during the English Civil War and the Jacobite Risings - balances out his singularly unhappy experience with Don Sebastian.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not hard to imagine him forging friendships with the Franco-Scottish Toreador, but also easy to imagine these friendships in becoming rather conflicted after the Second Anarch Revolt (Incidentally, it\u2019s intriguing to wonder if it was MacNeil\u2019s sometime association with the Toreador that pointed him in the direction of Los Angeles in the first place - as opposed to San Francisco, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> (3) I had not realised that there was, canonically, a Setite convert actually in MacNeil\u2019s coterie - my notion of Nicholas as a non-Setite member of the Cult of Set was grounded more in the basic facts that Nicholas had kept something of the Cult<br /> of Set going between the First &amp; Second Temples, that his leadership dispute with Dawn was not really explained and that he was brought down after MacNeil became involved in this dispute.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, it struck me as interesting to wonder whether the origin of this dispute could have lain in the divide between a Setite of the Clan proper and a \u2018mere\u2019 convert.<br /> <br /> <br /> (4) Incidentally, I definitely think it makes more sense to keep the Setite member of MacNeil\u2019s coterie a going concern - it\u2019s a<br /> logical plot hook, especially for a mole hunt of the TINKER, TAILOR, SOLDIER, SPY sort (As well as a desperately needed asset for the Setites, very much of the sort required to keep them viable in LA after two failures within fifty years).<br /> <br /> For my money the most interesting interpretation of this Brujah\u2019s conversion might be the desire to see the Anarch Revolution not only replace the previous political order, but supplant the Road of Humanity with something more \u2026 vampire (But less blatantly dysfunctional than an Anarch\u2019s understanding of the Sabbat).<br /> <br /> So this person would be a convert very much of the sort sought out by Hesha Rubadze - someone who converted not merely with appetite for decadence, but with an interest in transgressing and surpassing conventional Kindred morality (An aspiration distinct from the classic Brujah approach, but not so very alien to their combination of rebellious spirit and occasional investment in higher philosophies).<br /> <br /> <br /> (4) For the record, my understanding is that the \u2018Second Temple\u2019 period occurred during the early-to-mid 1960s, possibly in parallel to the Sabbat infiltrations: if nothing else, this would definitely keep storylines in LA swinging (Like a heavyweight with a grudge, in fact).<br /> <br /> <br /> (5) Finally, it\u2019s interesting to note that while Dawn is a remarkable survivor, there\u2019s a case to be made that she\u2019s grown a bit gun shy after her repeated failures in LA - my impression is that she\u2019s an extremely capable subversive, but not very good at growing her organisation (Possibly because all her training and early experience involved bringing down elements within the European colonial powers, an aristocratic culture and political situation rather different to the one prevailing in the United States of America, at least in Los Angeles: perhaps to some degree she still thinks in \u2018Top Down\u2019 rather than \u2018Grass roots\u2019).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T11:39:49-08:00","id":1548913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548909#post1548909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One interesting question having over the exact membership of the MacNeil Boys is whether Jeremy MacNeil\u2019s past alignment with Clan Toreador - specifically during the English Civil War and the Jacobite Risings - balances out his singularly unhappy experience with Don Sebastian.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not hard to imagine him forging friendships with the Franco-Scottish Toreador, but also easy to imagine these friendships in becoming rather conflicted after the Second Anarch Revolt (Incidentally, it\u2019s intriguing to wonder if it was MacNeil\u2019s sometime association with the Toreador that pointed him in the direction of Los Angeles in the first place - as opposed to San Francisco, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make sense that MacNeil had old Scottish Toreador allies when he was fighting the English Ventrue. I imagine it's more the local Brujah who associate the Toreador with Camarilla rule and oppression because of Don Sebastian, but that's become part of the local LA scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548909#post1548909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, it struck me as interesting to wonder whether the origin of this dispute could have lain in the divide between a Setite of the Clan proper and a \u2018mere\u2019 convert.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is certainly possible. The Setites do want to convert other vampires to the ways of Set. At the same time, I can't see them ever allowing someone who does not have the blood of Set to actually lead one of their temples. I don't think that scenario has ever been discussed in any sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548909#post1548909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I definitely think it makes more sense to keep the Setite member of MacNeil\u2019s coterie a going concern - it\u2019s a<br /> logical plot hook, especially for a mole hunt of the TINKER, TAILOR, SOLDIER, SPY sort (As well as a desperately needed asset for the Setites, very much of the sort required to keep them viable in LA after two failures within fifty years).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree that having a Setite mole present would make the setting a lot more interesting. There's actually a lot of intriguing things about the Setite operation in Los Angeles. It's a more obvious hook than a Sabbat or Camarilla invasion because either would likely blow up a lot of the setting (which can be fun, but also requires a lot more work by the ST to determine the aftereffects) while a plot involving the Setites would allow the ST to keep much of the setting intact as is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548909#post1548909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my money the most interesting interpretation of this Brujah\u2019s conversion might be the desire to see the Anarch Revolution not only replace the previous political order, but supplant the Road of Humanity with something more \u2026 vampire (But less blatantly dysfunctional than an Anarch\u2019s understanding of the Sabbat).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an intriguing option. One bit in the book is that a lot of Brujah Idealists are disappointed that MacNeil did not attempt once again to make a &quot;new&quot; Carthage and fulfill all the ideals of the clan. They're not really happy with the Free States, That one of MacNeil's mates might be in that persuasion (and somehow sees the Setite philosophy (or support) as a way to realize Carthage 3.0) is an interesting path. It would also make an interesting way that the second temple was different from the first as Dawn altered her approach from a Toreador ruled Camarilla to a Brujah ruled Free State.<br /> <br /> Now I'm wondering if I have should have kind of New Carthage Debating Society among the Brujah for those who are less concerned about the Anarch Movement per se than establishing their Brujah Utopia. It would also make a good in with the coterie of foreign Brujah Idealists &quot;studying&quot; the free states.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1548909#post1548909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, my understanding is that the \u2018Second Temple\u2019 period occurred during the early-to-mid 1960s, possibly in parallel to the Sabbat infiltrations: if nothing else, this would definitely keep storylines in LA swinging (Like a heavyweight with a grudge, in fact).</div> </div> </div> </div>The sourcebook gives 1969 as the year Dawn established her second temple. I'll discuss this more in a new thread specifically about the Setites. I might start that one next since we're already talking about it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-04T04:34:06-08:00","id":1548946,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, since they\u2019re not all Setite related I\u2019ll reply to your points above in this thread, then move all Snake-related discussions to the appropriate thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> (1) At least back in the days of the <i>Ancien Regime</i>, I\u2019d bet that keeping allies amongst the Scottish Toreador meant having more than one friend in France - it amuses me to imagine that a key point of personal tension between MacNeil and Germaine would be the former\u2019s record of cooperation with the sort of Kindred who would have liked to see Germaine torn apart by wild horses (Though the fact these cooperations were directed against the \u2018English\u2019 might slightly mitigate this).<br /> <br /> <br /> (2) It\u2019s not hard to imagine Los Angeles Toreador - whether of Don Sebastian\u2019s bloodline or not - being famously discrete (At least by Toreador standards) or famously open-handed when it comes to bribing the local Anarchs with \u2018Bread &amp; Circuses\u2019.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I tend to believe that Isaac Abrams - of BLOODLINES - would most likely be a grandchilde of Don Sebastian* (Mostly because the Prince of LA seems to have placed an emphasis on \u2018Spanish\u2019 blood, which suggests that he would limit his personal embraces to those who possessed it, but might well have been shrewd enough to command his own childe to embrace a Yankee or two to act as a \u2018face\u2019 and/or mouthpiece in an increasingly Anglo city.<br /> <br /> In other words, one assumes that Isaac Abrams is - or ought to be - of the Eighth Generation (Presumably embraced about twenty years before the Second Anarch revolt, possibly discretely).<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*Much to my amusement, I\u2019ve only just realised that the first and (In one version of events) second Prince of LA have exactly the same Christian name - amusing mental image of Smiling Jack claiming that nobody else noticed this \u2018cause Don Sebastian\u2019s first name was \u2018Don\u2019 obviously - which can hardly have been a good omen for the success of Prince Sebastian LaCroix.<br /> <br /> Honestly, somebody on the Camarilla must have wanted him dead \u2018Aut Caesar aut nihil\u2019.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> (3) I agree that it\u2019s unlikely that the Clan Setite proper would let mere converts hold the reins of power in the Cult of Set, which is why it struck me that depicting the Free States as somewhere the situation was fluid and unconventional enough for exactly that sort of situation to arise would be a useful opportunity to explore a probably-unprecedented scenario.<br /> <br /> If not through Nicholas then through the Brujah mole in MacNeil\u2019s coterie.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I\u2019m pleased to learn that this would, in fact, appear to be a situation without precedent in the literature - if you can\u2019t find the unprecedented in the Anarch Free States from time to time, then where?<br /> <br /> <br /> (4) Incidentally, given that Gloria appears to have been resident in San Francisco between the first and second Temple periods (There\u2019s an interesting tale or two to be told there, I suspect - this is the Peak Film Noir era and San Francisco has significant associations with the genre - given that Prince Vannevar Thomas runs a tight ship and Setites love to shake things loose), it\u2019s possible that Nicholas was the one who kept the Followers of Set working in LA, suggesting that it could well have been HIM who put the Word of Set into our Brujah convert\u2019s ear.<br /> <br /> <br /> (5) I\u2019d bet that the subject of \u2018New Carthage\u2019 Utopianism has been discussed ad nauseum in private gatherings, though one suspects it\u2019s the sort of thing brought up at local Rabts only to receive a decidedly-mixed (and possibly confused) reception.<br /> <br /> Mental image of Smiling Jack only just barely refraining from shooting the notion down with extreme prejudice - all the better to hear Johnny Brujah and Billy Anarch ask sterling questions like \u201cWhere\u2019s a Carthage and why should we ****ing care?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> (6) That shoots my vague mental image of the timeline all to pieces, but it does suggest that there could have been a connection between the Sabbat Incursion and the second Temple - presumably the Setites slithered in through the gaps in Anarch ranks left by the shovelheads et al.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T10:41:50-07:00","id":1549158,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, out of curiosity, where do you imagine the BLOODLINES characters sitting, generation-wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T17:12:33-07:00","id":1549171,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I have never played Bloodlines, and all I know about that computer game is what little I have read on the White Wolf Wiki. Since I view most of those characters as disposable filler, I'll be treating them as I do any NPCs I create from the template descriptions of the clanbooks. Which is assigning their generation fairly randomly between 8 through 13 except when I cobble together a few of them as lineages of sire-childe-grandchilde-etc. and need to assign appropriate generation to everyone. <br /> <br /> When there is already an assigned generation, I'll likely keep with that. For example, I think Therese/Jeanette Voermann is supposed to be the childe of Jacob/Esau from Milwaukee By Night so I'll default her generation based on his. However, since I've long though Jacob/Esau's canon generation is far too strong (and in fact, possibly a typo), I'll lower it to something I think is more appropriate.<br /> <br /> Since I think the Free States act as a &quot;haven&quot; for the relatively weak among Kindred, I'll put more weight on weaker generations like 10-13, but there will be some with stronger generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T11:09:48-07:00","id":1549195,"title":"","content":"Yes I can see most Anarchs being of the 12th-13th generation with a decent smattering of 10th-11th generation anciliea with the odd member of the 9th generation Kindred hanging around. Anything above the 9th generation is pushing it inhmo as they would have greater potential power and usually have some measure of influence in the Camarilla sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-12T13:27:27-07:00","id":1549202,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, thank you most kindly for answering my latest query!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T18:33:39-07:00","id":1549433,"title":"","content":"I'm considering whether to include the Gangrel Valkyries as cast members of the chronicle. LABN does not include any Gangrel at all, and there's only a few Gangrel ever mentioned in regard to the Free States. However, in Clanbook Gangrel Revised it is mentioned that there are now four Gangrel Valkyrie on the West Coast. It's part of the Revised metaplot where the Free States no longer exist, the Cathayan vampires for some reason have conquered Los Angeles, and now four powerful elder Gangrel are there to fight them. There's probably a Death Star, Agent Smith, and John Wick involved as well for all I know.<br /> <br /> It's anachronistic to include any Valkyries at the time of the original sourcebook, but I'm only using canon as inspiration here. Using some of my other ideas about the All High and his followers (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe\">located in the Werewolf forum here</a>), there's no reason why a group of four Valkyrie wouldn't be sent to North America. And given their hostility to the Toreador and Ventrue (and the Camarilla), it would make sense for them to use the Free States as a safe haven as they travel North America on secret assignment for whatever macguffins they're given.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, there's no details given whatsoever on these four Valkyries except that they're all blonde and big on teaching people Viking ways. So I'll becoming up with characters from scratch.<br /> <br /> I'm more interested on what I can do with them in the chronicle. First, they aren't actually anarchs even if they have common enemies in the Camarilla. As explicit followers of the All High who are part of an army preparing for Gehenna, they don't have anything in common with MacNeil or the Anarch Movement. The Valkyries just find the anarchs to be convenient allies. Still, I can have fun with the idea of the PCs and other NPCs learning this. They're just another group with their own agenda exploiting the Free States while they can. Second, they are another possible source of magic among the Anarchs, and this is something I'd like to explore. The All High knows blood magic, and so do some of his followers. Having one Valkyrie know some old school magic (like Weather Control or Neptune's Might) that could potentially be taught to some worthy other (who wants to help Odin in Ragnarok!) could be an intriguing option. Third, they can be potential allies or enemies to the PCs as they do whatever it is they're doing (for Odin IC, for whatever reason I want them to do OOC) and the PCs come across them. They could become a convenient quest giver especially for more esoteric or unusual scenarios.<br /> <br /> I think a group of four Nordic vampire beauties (all speaking English with a pronounced Norse accent and making common language mistakes as speakers of English as a foreign language) are probably going to be hits among PCs. While World of Darkness puts Brunnhilde herself as riding a Harley-Davidson, I'm more inclined to give these four a European cruiser motorcycle. (I think they need cruisers if they intend to travel throughout much of North America). The Moto Gussi California was not only in production at the time, but used by the LAPD and CHP. Of course, if people who know motorcycles suggest a better option, I'll take it.<br /> <br /> I'll not have them be in LA when the chronicle begins, but may introduce them as arriving after the PCs have established themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T13:17:47-07:00","id":1549462,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d suspect that Smiling Jack would take a close interest in these professional rivals - as I recall, you suggested making him point man for an Anarch counterpart to the Camarilla motorbike rangers in the Midwest - and one also believes that you should be careful not to go too far when it comes to the Valkyries\u2019 difficulties with English (It\u2019s always wise to temper the World of Darkness with shots of black comedy and more genuine humour, but can be overdone, especially when it comes to something as larger than life as a motorcycle club of vampire valkyries).<br /> <br /> It would also be important to make sure that each Valkyrie has individual features of interest to mark her out from her sisters, at least for those who keep a careful eye out: for example, one may have trouble with English because she learned it in Saxon England and keeps tripping over the Great Vowel Shift (Amongst other recent complexities); another has more difficulty accepting that people are STILL hung up on that whole \u2018Christianity\u2019 thing (Having become thoroughly converted to \u2018Odinism\u2019 after seeing Catholics &amp; Protestants do themselves no credit in the Thirty Years War) and yet another does her best to be Peak Viking despite being not much older than ABBA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T23:04:19-07:00","id":1549474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1549462#post1549462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would also be important to make sure that each Valkyrie has individual features of interest to mark her out from her sisters, at least for those who keep a careful eye out:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not exactly sure how to proceed here. As originally written, the Valkyries seem to have vanished sometime after the Christianization of Scandinavia and the arrival of Ventrue and Toreador into the region and took over the place from the Brujah and Gangrel who were previously there, and then appeared once again in the seventies or eighties (likely awakening from some kind of self-induced torpor). So the original Valkyries are probably between 1000-2000 years old, and any new ones would be recruited only in the last ten or twenties years (counting from a chronicle beginning in the 1990s). Since loyalty to Odin/the All High would be a pre-requisite, I imagine any new neonates must be taken from the Norse neopagan community and then properly groomed for service.<br /> <br /> It might make sense for two of the four to be elders, and the other two to be their relatively recent childer. The neonates could each help their sire navigate the modern world (and speak fluent English) while the elders would be in charge of the mission. An easy way to distinguish the elders would be to have them from different time periods and different places. Maybe one from the classic Viking Age from Norway or Sweden, and the other from an earlier pre-viking age like the time of Beowulf or Anglo-Saxon invasion of Britain (6th century) in Denmark. Then assign some differing personality quirks and interests to each one.<br /> <br /> I'll probably have the two neonates act as the front to the PCs and other characters. I think that may cause PCs to think those are the &quot;leaders&quot;. I'll have to wait to see if the misdirection works.<br /> <br /> I want a spread of generation so maybe one group if generation 7/8 and the other 10/11.<br /> <br /> One problem I generally have with elder Gangrel is figuring out how many and what kind of animalistic features they should show. This is something usually neglected in the sourcebooks, but I feel is quite necessary when you have Gangrel characters. Rather than going with lupine features, which is my standard go to, I'm thinking of one having ravenlike features (because of ravens association with Odin) and one with feline features (because cats are sacred to Freya, the other receiver of the einheriar). I'm not so worried about the neonates since they're so young we can either assume they have no animalistic features or ones that are easily covered up.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T00:22:21-07:00","id":1549475,"title":"","content":"You could possibly have one of the Valkyria be from some isolated northern community where the cult still has a foothold via ghouls and the like (maybe with a slumbering elder being tapped for ritual vitae). It's also entirely possible that some cult like that might've transplanted itself to North America during the wave of Scandinavian immigration. Perhaps even a rough cycle where every couple of hundred years, the elder Valkyria picks a new protege to embrace and oversee the cult, and sends the previous protege off with some ghouls and a herd to establish a new branch cult somewhere. <br /> This could result in having one of the AFS group be a newly awakened elder from the old country (perhaps with a relatively younger assistant a guide to the modern world), with another being a hundred-something year old from Minnesota that was sent out to California ten or twenty years ago and currently has a newly embraced local protege.<br /> <br /> As for animal features, ravens, falcons, and other birds of prey are probably the best choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T12:31:53-07:00","id":1549487,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, it would probably be a good idea to show some of the Valkyries with non-Asgardian animal features (To make it more plain that The Allfather only claims to be Odin) - or a mix of Asgardian and non Asgardian animal elements - whilst showing those with \u2018proper\u2019 bestial features favoured over those with features less readily associated with the Norse deities.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d bet that those with lupine features are treated with particular ambivalence, given the Get of Fenrir\u2019s ancient grudge and the long war stemming from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T20:10:05-07:00","id":1549511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1549475#post1549475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could possibly have one of the Valkyria be from some isolated northern community where the cult still has a foothold via ghouls and the like (maybe with a slumbering elder being tapped for ritual vitae). It's also entirely possible that some cult like that might've transplanted itself to North America during the wave of Scandinavian immigration. Perhaps even a rough cycle where every couple of hundred years, the elder Valkyria picks a new protege to embrace and oversee the cult, and sends the previous protege off with some ghouls and a herd to establish a new branch cult somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is true and that even goes along with what I developed on the Werewolf forum. That would insure certain allegiances in terms of embracing someone they know will follow the part. I already planned for a certain kind of survivalist compound controlled by the cult to be located somewhere in Southern California so that PCs could have somewhere nearby to go in case they get involved with this group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1549475#post1549475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This could result in having one of the AFS group be a newly awakened elder from the old country (perhaps with a relatively younger assistant a guide to the modern world), with another being a hundred-something year old from Minnesota that was sent out to California ten or twenty years ago and currently has a newly embraced local protege.</div> </div> </div> </div>That or something similar makes sense. Not only would each elder have one neonate to guide them, but one of the neonates - being American - could better help them adjust to being in the US. She'd know certain cultural marks that a Swede (or whomever) wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-22T22:27:28-07:00","id":1549517,"title":"","content":"It also occurs to me that one of the pairs could be passing themselves off as some sort of New Age hippy-era holdover neopagan mystical sect, while the other pair have assembled a collection of bikers, metal heads, and other outlaw types. <br /> <br /> Regarding the latter, there is a somewhat obscure movie from 1986 called <i>Nomads</i>. It is an odd film, one of the first from the guy who IIRC went on to direct Predator, featuring Pierce Brosnan as an LA anthropologist who stumbles across a gang of modern day urban nomads who are not entirely what they seem. It's a bit uneven but does have a lot of interesting 80s LA scenery that goes well with LA by Night, and the gang make good visual inspiration for a general sort of Anarch coterie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-23T00:44:56-07:00","id":1549518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1549517#post1549517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also occurs to me that one of the pairs could be passing themselves off as some sort of New Age hippy-era holdover neopagan mystical sect, while the other pair have assembled a collection of bikers, metal heads, and other outlaw types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I intend the Valkyries to show up a little after the PCs first arrive, they'll be brand new to the Anarch Free States when they first arrive. However, it's not a bad idea that after they arrive and orient themselves, that they may not specialize in different activities on behalf of Odin. Whether the PCs actually discover this is up to them. While I do run specific plots for the PCs so they have something obvious to do every game session, I like sandbox style settings where the PCs can decide to do whatever motivates them in the setting. So exploring what the Valkyrie are actually up to will probably be more of a sandbox thing that requires the PCs to be interested in them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1549517#post1549517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the latter, there is a somewhat obscure movie from 1986 called <i>Nomads</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have absolutely no memory of this film, and after reading its synopsis on Wikipedia, I'll be unlikely to watch it. But from its trailer, I agree it has some visuals that would be in place for LABN circa 1994.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zrnNbHRudWo\" data-code=\"zrnNbHRudWo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zrnNbHRudWo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-24T09:31:45-07:00","id":1549539,"title":"","content":"Man, Pierce Brosnan was and remains just annoyingly handsome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-24T19:01:20-07:00","id":1549548,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's always been something of a surprise to me that he does not have a bigger film career. Pretty much from the first few episodes of Remington Steele, people were saying he would make a great James Bond. And while he eventually did play James Bond, it took a decade longer than it should. Other than a few starring roles here and there, he's often cast in supporting roles. He obviously has a lot of screen credits and a successful career, but much like Rutger Hauer I expected him to have become a huge superstar. Enormously popular and liked by fans, but not someone who's had a career like Tom Hanks or Tom Cruise.<br /> <br /> = = =<br /> I want to talk about Edith and Enid Blount, in particular their diablerie. LABN indicates that they regularly diablerize lone Kindred who happen to fall into their clutches. Although they've been able to advance their generation from 12 to 10, most of their victims don't add to their generation at all. Since even one diablerie creates black stains on their aura for years, I imagine the vast majority of the time they've been around (or at least since 1944), their aura clearly marks them as diablerists.<br /> <br /> Their character description acknowledges this issue and says as an excuse the sisters claim they've needed to defend themselves and their territory from invaders. However, defending themselves by killing Kindred trespassers is not the same as diablerizing them. The writer of LABN clearly wants the extent of the sisters' crimes to be somewhat of a mystery, but I can't see how much of a mystery this is for anyone who has auspex and been around a significant amount of time. I certainly don't think any PCs will have trouble putting together the Blount sisters as their primary suspect once they hear how many Kindred have mysteriously disappeared around Glendale (despite the Lupine threat also being prominent here). It would just make all the other Kindred of LA to be incredibly stupid to not figure it out as well.<br /> <br /> So is there anything that can be done to revive this, or introduce any kind of mystery or suspense? Or introduce some sort of doubt among PCs that the Blount sisters aren't actually horrifying monsters? While not important characters, they are interesting enough flavor I want to include them in some ongoing capacity. As is, I only see the PCs either completely avoiding them, or ending them in short order. If the PCs do destroy the Blount sisters, I want it to be a real decision for the characters, and not done simply because it's the &quot;obvious&quot; thing to do. Plus I've always loved Arsenic and Old Lace.<br /> <br /> Also, what should be done about their Humanity? Like a lot of callous and dangerous Kindred in early sourcebooks, they are given a Humanity of 0. However, this was before the game settled on Humanity zero vampires degenerating into wights, and no matter how wights might be portrayed, the Blount sisters clearly have enough mental capacity that they aren't that. So what should we do? Simply make them stable, but low 2-3 Humanity vampires? Put them on some kind of Path, possibly one they obtained from a captured Sabbat they cannibalized back in 1965? If so, what Path? Make them secret infernalists on the Path of Evil Revelations? Make them low, but stable members of the Path of Typhon by making them Kindred secretly recruited by the Setites earlier? They may not be any higher on the Path of Typhon than Humanity, but I imagine they'd be less likely to become wights if on a path.<br /> <br /> The Blount sisters clearly destroyed their own father/sire in 1927 only three years after their embrace, but there is no reason to think they cannibalized other Kindred during the rule of Don Sebastian. They might have still murdered many mortals by their deceptions since this may just be part of their normal hunting method, but I think they would have only moved onto diablerie after the Free States were established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T12:31:30-07:00","id":1549562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, it's always been something of a surprise to me that he does not have a bigger film career. Pretty much from the first few episodes of Remington Steele, people were saying he would make a great James Bond. And while he eventually did play James Bond, it took a decade longer than it should. Other than a few starring roles here and there, he's often cast in supporting roles. He obviously has a lot of screen credits and a successful career, but much like Rutger Hauer I expected him to have become a huge superstar. Enormously popular and liked by fans, but not someone who's had a career like Tom Hanks or Tom Cruise. </div> </div> </div> Clearly his career was savagely handicapped by his not having been christened \u2018Tom\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the Blount sisters, the answer to that question really revolves around how common the \u2018Auspex\u2019 ability happens to be and how likely two little old lady vampires are to attract close attention from Interested parties - I suspect their being relatively quiet monsters has played a key role in keeping them a going concern, coupled with what I suspect to be a deeply policing-averse wider community in the Anarch Free States (Itself violent enough to produce a significant casualty rate for young, friendless vampires whom very few would miss).<br /> <br /> If nothing else, if lonely vampires go missing in the vicinity of two well-established members of the Kindred community, locals would presume murder and not outright diablerie (Especially if the sisters have long experience of properly disposing of their victims), which means they might well have avoided being subject to the old \u2018Soul Gaze\u2019 to date.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for keeping them relevant, one of the more entertaining methods wouod be to set them up as the resident cross between Jessica Fletcher and Hannibal Lecter - little old ladies with a spectacularly sharp nose for murder and other homicide related mysteries who are just delighted to share their expertise (\u201cahem, sensible ideas and long experience\u201d) with coteries of an enquiring mind.<br /> <br /> Given there are two sisters, you might do worse than to give one low Humanity and the other a non-Humanity Path, if only because this gives these two Old Lady Vampires something to talk about!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T15:12:41-07:00","id":1549568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1549562#post1549562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Blount sisters, the answer to that question really revolves around how common the \u2018Auspex\u2019 ability happens to be and how likely two little old lady vampires are to attract close attention from Interested parties - I suspect their being relatively quiet monsters has played a key role in keeping them a going concern, coupled with what I suspect to be a deeply policing-averse wider community in the Anarch Free States (Itself violent enough to produce a significant casualty rate for young, friendless vampires whom very few would miss).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's enough for it to be something easily known after a few decades. Aura Perception is just Auspex 2. Lots of clans have it, and it tends to be a fairly popular Discipline even for Kindred for whom it is an out-of-clan Discipline. A quick eyeball survey of LABN shows about 15 NPCs have it, and CBN1e has about 30 NPCs with it. It's between 1/3 to 1/2 of all named characters with stats in those sourcebooks. Now the WoD is notorious for wanky NPC stats that don't make sense, and once the ST throws in his own NPCs that can go down. But it seems to be a fairly prevalent power. It won't be on all the time, but since diablerie stains last for years and the Blount sisters seem to practice it regularly, it'll get noticed at some point. And once one person notices, the news should spread and it's easily confirmed.<br /> <br /> Now if all the Blount sisters do is stay in Glendale and never come out, that'll be easier to miss. But then you have almost zero chance of PCs running into them unless the STs send them on a chase that causes them to directly interact with the Blounts. I'm not fond of that approach personally. I'd prefer a more natural interaction. Some early interaction with the sisters first just to introduce the character. Then at some point have some minor NPC they befriend just disappear, and if the PCs investigate they'll learn the last place he was seen was around Glendale. And then everything after that depends on what the PCs do, if anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1549562#post1549562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If nothing else, if lonely vampires go missing in the vicinity of two well-established members of the Kindred community, locals would presume murder and not outright diablerie (Especially if the sisters have long experience of properly disposing of their victims), which means they might well have avoided being subject to the old \u2018Soul Gaze\u2019 to date.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally I agree, but at least in canon those disappearances are noteworthy. It gets mentioned in several places in the sourcebook, leaving a bit of a mystery until you get to the Blount sisters character description and then the reason why becomes obvious.<br /> <br /> And there's enough NPCs who should have learned about the diablerie stains over the past few decades that someone should make the connection. One can ignore black stains that last a few years and go away, but it's harder to do that if they keep lasting for decades.<br /> <br /> Now it's possible to say that the Kindred of LA just don't care enough about diablerie to do anything about it. But even then, I imagine there has to at least be some small group of Kindred who would just say, &quot;Fuck it, let's lynch mob them&quot; at some point, and then it'll be over for the Blount sisters. (Even if all the Kinded who disappear are insignificant loners or newcomers without strong ties to others, I think at some point a small, but sufficient, mob forms since it's just these two insignificant Toreador who also lack others who would protect them.) Who is really going to defend them or retaliate in vengeance afterwards? Edward Vignes might initially, but any mention of decades lasting diablerie stains would probably cause him to back down.<br /> <br /> So my preference would be some way that the Blounts can somehow hide their stains. It might not be 100% effective or available all the time, but enough that it can drop suspicions. (PCs may be able to see it successfully, and maybe someone mentions that back in the day they knew at least one of the sisters had black stains.) Maybe it's some Sabbat relic the sisters obtained during the Sabbat invasion. Or some very rare Anarch Blood Magic ritual that hides it somehow, or the effect of a demonic investment because of a pact made to some demon. If someone know a canonical item or ritual that can accomplish this, I'm interested in knowing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-25T21:27:59-07:00","id":1549575,"title":"","content":"In hindsight, it feels like there should have been a way to use Obfuscate to hide the signs of vampire cannibalism. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T12:03:08-07:00","id":1549595,"title":"","content":"How odd: this forum has noted that there\u2019s a PETRODON AND THE CAMARILLA thread, but when I click on it the site denies me access and when I view the MASQUERADE sub-forum there\u2019s no sign of the thread.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I salute you, a thread that does and does not exist represents some Very Serious commitment to evoking the full World of Darkness experience.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T13:08:26-07:00","id":1549598,"title":"","content":"The first post on the new thread is held up for approval. After posting I foolishly edited it to correct a typo, and it immediately put it in limbo. When a moderator finally gets around to approving it, I'm sure it'll reappear.<br /> <br /> I'm sure Petrodon himself would approve of a thread about him that is simultaneously there but cannot be seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T14:36:51-07:00","id":1549602,"title":"","content":"If anything can make that happen, it\u2019s THE Clan of Vampire Computer Nerds (Clearly the latest cinematic achievement of Mr Robert Eggars has made them bold: we\u2019ll have to threaten them with the ghost of Mrs Florence Stoker to teach them some proper caution AND scare them back to their hopes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-28T17:32:54-07:00","id":1549623,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat heading away from actual anarchs to a sourcebook that on the surface has no connection to the Free States, 1999's Time of Thin Blood. Despite a lot of disdain I have for the Revised period, it did produce some good materials and interesting ideas. I think this sourcebook is one of them, mostly because the issue of what comes after the 13th generation was always a big question ever since the game was introduced.<br /> <br /> Some of the concepts introduced here I feel are very appropriate for a Free States chronicle because if any place would provide a critical mass for them, it would have to be the Free States. One can understand that Princes, almost unanimously, would simply prohibit any known 13th generation vampire from siring, even someone like Modius. There is nothing to stop them in Los Angeles. It would also be a haven for any thin blooded vampires that were illegally embraced and now fleeing for their lives. The Free States are the perfect place to introduce and deal with these kind of issues.<br /> <br /> So the first thing is just having a noticeable amount of 14th and 15th generation vampires around. I think some - especially those of the 14th generation - can be integrated into many of the existing coteries and gangs. Many anarchs won't care whatsoever the official generation of Kindred or even ask (or know what they are themselves). And while the anarch gangs do prioritize combat strength for their own street wars, the bog standard 14th generation vampire may not appear to be any physically weaker than the vast majority of other neonates. And some Thin Bloods could prove themselves very useful. ToTB introduces the concept of Thin Blood &quot;seers&quot; who have a unique mystic Background Insight that produces supernatural visions and premonitions of intrigues of the elder. Wouldn't that be useful to the anarchs? I'll be introducing one 14th generation vampire who has strong Insight that was recruited by Jeremy MacNeil into his personal coterie, and she's extremely thankful for having such powerful and influential allies/protectors.<br /> <br /> Those who do seem much weaker - those 14th gen with the Thin Blood flaw, the 15th gen, or those with additional Flaws associated with Thin Blood - might be isolated or forced to join together only among themselves. I wonder if such Thin Bloods often become victims of Kindred like the Blount sisters. While &quot;officially&quot; anarchs shouldn't care about this, I think most do. Some of this might be residual prejudice - especially from the older anarchs, but I think more often this would be simply more dangerous predators sensing weakness and seeking to prey on the weak. That is especially the case in an overcrowded domain where feeding competition becomes fierce.<br /> <br /> To me, the main question is how many Thin Bloods should be in Los Angeles, and how do other Kindred interact with them, particularly those who might prey on them. All together the great LA metro area probably has between 150-200 vampires. I am thinking keeping the Thin Bloods between 5-10 in number, although who that is may change as old ones disappear and new ones arrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-28T17:41:08-07:00","id":1549624,"title":"","content":"The other concept in ToTB that I'll be using is the idea of the Unbound. The Unbound is simply &quot;a loose social movement&quot; who reject the entire concept of clans entirely. If this idea is ever to gain critical mass that it spreads to many domains, it has to begin in the Free States. I can't imagine it is ever going to get any traction in a traditional domain when anarchs have more pressing issues to deal with and often have to make deals with elders opposed to the Prince just to get some breathing room.<br /> <br /> So I am going to make &quot;The Unbound&quot; the name of an actual gang/coterie. So many places in LA are simply labelled as &quot;gang of 10 Kindred&quot; or &quot;gang of 15 Kindred&quot;, so giving these small, completely undefined, gangs a real identity is so important. It's primarily a gang of Brujah and Caitiff but may have a Malkavian in it. I think the other clans may be too protective of their identity, but I might have more Kindred of different clans join later on in the chronicle.<br /> <br /> The members are very weak generation and very young, so they don't see the reason for the importance of clans. If they become friends with vampire X, why should that Kindred's genealogy matter? Clans are just another tool of the elders to divide the young, aren't they? Their homespun philosophy would be quickly crushed in any other domain, but they are able to create their own philosophy and propagandize it in the Free States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T15:20:33-07:00","id":1549687,"title":"","content":"You know I\u2019m a Camarilla player at heart when the very notion of some young-bloods dismissing the Clan Structure reduces me to a tizzy of Old World outrage and haughty disdain - good glory, next thing you know they\u2019ll be insisting that Count Dracula start calling himself \u2018Dear Leader\u2019 not \u2018Prince of Darkness\u2019.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On a more serious note, the Free States definitely makes sense as the hub for those thin-bloods who don\u2019t fancy their chances with the Sabbat: it occurs to me that you could easily tie this movement to Amethyst\u2019s efforts to oust Allison Maller (With Tom Weaver as her more socially-acceptable figurehead).<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve wondered for some time if this struggle for Anaheim represents a case of vampires with nothing but \u2018family connections\u2019 to call their own looking for a place to get out from under their Sires and crashing headlong into the genuine untouchables of Kindred society (Who lack just about everything except the wit to recognise that by tackling Salvador Garcia\u2019s youngest Childe, they can tap into rivalries that will encourage more powerful Kindred to do at least some<br /> of their fighting for them - possibly even to the extent of waging a proxy war).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T18:14:19-07:00","id":1549693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1549687#post1549687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, the Free States definitely makes sense as the hub for those thin-bloods who don\u2019t fancy their chances with the Sabbat: it occurs to me that you could easily tie this movement to Amethyst\u2019s efforts to oust Allison Maller (With Tom Weaver as her more socially-acceptable figurehead).</div> </div> </div> </div>I will definitely be making the contest for Anaheim between ideological factions rather than just random vampires fighting for turf whose only distinction is which personality is leading a group of unknown and undefined vampires. I simply don't find Alison Maller, Tom Weaver, and Amethyst to be particularly interesting as characters, know why any PC would pick one over the other, or why it really matters if Amethyst wins.<br /> <br /> I'll keep their names and general description, but making each of their &quot;gangs&quot; distinct. Even if the PCs don't get involved, at least when one side wins, it'll have an impact to the setting. If the PCs helped one side when versus the other, they'll have a feeling of accomplishment. If they stay out, then maybe they'll one day regret not intervening, or at least have to deal with the consequences.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T19:24:35-07:00","id":1549698,"title":"","content":"This was a duplicate for some reason even though it was not what I actually posted. It just reposted what I wrote an hour earlier for some reason. When I have free time, I might rewrite what I actually wrote. Must be some strange glitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 04-02-2025, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T04:02:24-07:00","id":1550144,"title":"","content":"This is what happens when you get too interested in Clan Nosferatu: Shreck.net decides to make some mischief at your expense!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T00:26:17-07:00","id":1550654,"title":"","content":"There is a mention of an &quot;evangelical anarch&quot; named Laecanus in the Anarch Cookbook. It's in the same section on philosophy that mentions perspectives on diablerie and Libertas. It's part of the same mess of gnosticism that pervades a lot of early WoD and Vampire. Laecanus proclaims a &quot;new moral perspective&quot; on Caine. Basically, the villain is God and Caine was unjustly punished. Since he was punished unjustly, all vampires are also unjustly punished. That frenzy where you killed all those people? Not your fault. The blame is on God.<br /> <br /> Laecanus believes that is Kindred can just absolve themselves of any guilt, they can free themselves of frenzy since their cause is external. It's just another strange belief that is not supported by game mechanics, but as a philosophy in the setting it does have some internal logic. However, I can't see this as possibly working. Someone who tries to feel no guilt at all is just going to fuel the Beast and let him take over.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of oddball anarch characters mentioned in the Anarch Cookbook and elsewhere, the best place to put this character is in the Free States. It's another missed opportunity of LABN that it did not include him. This is the kind of thing that can make an interesting NPC for the PCs to interact with.<br /> <br /> However, as far as I know there is nothing else known about this character. We get just one paragraph. The most likely clans for him would either be Brujah or Malkavian. His theory is so outlandish it would be easy to just label him Malkavian. However, then it'd be too easy to dismiss in my opinion. The Brujah are supposed to be a clan of philosophers and radical thinkers, and I think this also fits in well with them.<br /> <br /> As &quot;apostle of Caine&quot; brings up connotations of the Path of Caine and thus the Sabbat, but I won't have this character be connected with them. Once you start with the idea that the first vampire was Cain, you are going to have ideas like this pop up independently. Sabbat on the Path of Caine might want to contact such a character if they hear about him, but I would prefer Laecanus to be sincere in his anarch loyalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T13:48:23-07:00","id":1550669,"title":"","content":"This is somewhat tangential but Laecanus\u2019 philosophy reminds me of an idea I\u2019ve been playing around with to flesh out the Sabbat\u2019s and other vampiro-gnostics positive reinterpretation of Caine, which may be somewhat useful here.<br /> <br /> If we look at Genesis and the punishments laid upon Adam &amp; Eve for eating the Fruit, what have we got? They are banished from the Garden, a land apparently without death or strife. Adam is punished by being forced to struggle with the earth for his sustenance. Eve is punished with subservience to Adam and the pains of childbirth (necessarily linked, particularly in the nascent agrarian states that Adam\u2019s new labors imply). Both are punished with mortality. <br /> <br /> Then let\u2019s look at their children. Interestingly we see the disdain laid upon Cain while praise is laid upon Abel. Now part of this has to do with the preference for pastoralism over sedentary agriculture (which itself is telling). However if we want to do a little amateur psychoanalysis it\u2019s not difficult to imagine that God\u2019s unfavorable response to Cain\u2019s offerings could also be reflective of Adam and Eve\u2019s animosity for Cain (who would represent for Adam a vision of himself as sedentary laborer, as opposed to his status in the Garden; and for Eve the living proof of her subordination to Adam and the pains of child-bearing). In contrast the pastoralist Abel is laden with favor, perhaps because of Cain\u2019s usefulness to his parents as scapegoat for their frustrations, perhaps because of pastoralism representing a break with sedentary agriculture, a sort of half step back to the implied Hunter-gatherer lifestyle of the Garden. <br /> <br /> Regardless Cain\u2019s frustration with his mistreatment (whether real or perceived) leads him to the murder of Abel (itself an interesting reflection of Abel\u2019s sacrifice of his flock of course) and by extension the invention of murder itself, here used in both a vengeful venting of spleen and presumably an attempt to take what was Abel\u2019s for himself (nominally his flock, in truth the approval and love of his parents/god).<br /> <br /> Now we take the pivot to vampire lore. <br /> <br /> If you look at what vampirism provides, you may notice something curious. It resembles a dark reflection of the Garden in some ways. Vampires are described as predators, but what does that mean in human terms, other than a return to a Hunter-gatherer lifestyle (sans the gathering)?<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s look at what else vampirism provides. It seems to provide a reversal of the punishments of the fall. Eve was punished by subordination to Adam and the pain of childbirth: as vampire has oft-pointed out the vampiric condition does not discriminate in sharing its gifts on basis of sex or gender, and furthermore the pains of human birth are replaced with the ecstasies of vampiric birth (both done in blood of course). Adam was punished with his harsh labors upon the earth, which the vampires are excused from, instead deriving their substance from the fruits of earthly living. Both were punished with mortality - which the vampire is definitionally excluded from.<br /> <br /> When one looks at vampirism from this perspective, particularly if one wants to add in a liberal dose of Lilith inflected Gnosticism, it doesn\u2019t seem too bizarre how vampires such as Laecanus or the Sabbat priesthood could justify Caine as a messianic figure and even extend this into a just rebellion against a tyrannical demiurge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-04T19:33:09-07:00","id":1550675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1550669#post1550669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now part of this has to do with the preference for pastoralism over sedentary agriculture (which itself is telling).</div> </div> </div> </div>I have long felt this particular interpretation to be extremely odd. While the narrative in the Bible is not explicit, I think there's a lot more obvious answers as to why God preferred Abel's sacrifice. I think emphasizing Cain's farming and Abel's shepherding as opposed to other elements in the story misses the point. But that debate is beyond the point of the game or this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1550669#post1550669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When one looks at vampirism from this perspective, particularly if one wants to add in a liberal dose of Lilith inflected Gnosticism, it doesn\u2019t seem too bizarre how vampires such as Laecanus or the Sabbat priesthood could justify Caine as a messianic figure and even extend this into a just rebellion against a tyrannical demiurge</div> </div> </div> </div>Once you place Cain as as the first vampire, certain ideas are going to come up.<br /> <br /> Of more importance is what kind of character should Laecanus be. Is he more of an intellectual and theologian speculating, or is he some kind of cult leader? He's called an evagelical anarch, but is he evangelical to this &quot;new moral perspective&quot; or the anarch cause? Did he develop this perspective after becoming an anarch, or did his speculations on the nature of Caine and the cursed cause the local Prince, or even Justicar and archons, to go after him and banish from polite Camarilla society? He's called a &quot;popular proponent&quot; of the idea, so he may not have invented it. He's just the best known Kindred to develop the idea and popularize it.<br /> <br /> Saying Caine was unjustly punished is not the same as being pro-Caine. After all, Caine created the Six Traditions. As an anarch, Laecanus likely does not believe they should be followed. Unlike the Sabbat that worships Caine because they believe he saved the early sect while in the guise of the Ravnos Methusaleh Vestgeir, there's no such story or legend among the anarchs. Caine is just another authority figure to be defied, not some daddy figure who is going to come in and save you from your older brothers picking on you. Caine may be a tragic or even sympathetic figure, but he is not necessarily someone to emulate.<br /> <br /> Instead, Laecanus is much more interested in eliminating frenzy (as a practical matter), and transferring the moral responsibility of a vampire's actions under frenzy onto a third person to eliminate the idea that vampires are evil. It seems like an excuse for vampires to do whatever they want - a get out of jail free card that lasts for all of eternity. Perhaps Laecanus does have some kind of moral code of his own, but he rejects the idea that vampires are simply evil per se. If an evil or unfortunate act comes from &quot;the Beast&quot;, the moral responsibility is not the vampire's. Presumably this is just one more thing the anarchs need to free themselves from. An ultimate expression of one's Libertas. Free yourself not just from political bondage, but spiritual bondage. &quot;I didn't ask for this, but I am going to free myself from this condition.&quot;<br /> <br /> This implies that Laecanus hopes somehow to eliminate or reduce &quot;the Beast&quot; inside vampires. Presumably the existential act of realizing the Beast is external to the vampire will either somehow remove it or put the vampire more in control of it. This is another way that Laecanus is different from the Sabbat which approves of any part of the vampire condition.<br /> <br /> Like some of the other elements in this philosophy section, the idea that a vampire can overcome one's own nature and weaknesses isn't developed in any mechanical sense in Vampire: the Masquerade. However, some of these ideas are found in the Ordo Dracul covenant in Vampire: The Requiem. While I am extremely reluctant to introduce anything like the Coils into the VtM setting, I think we may be able to steal some elements from the Ordo Dracul to Laecanus and his followers, especially in how Requiem/Ordo Dracul depict Dracula. Someone who may have dabbled in many things (blood magic, paths of enlightenment, noddism,) and found them wanting. He is now involved in the Great Work, an alchemy of the soul, the personal transcendence which will rescue his soul from the forces that bind it. The ultimate act of liberation.<br /> <br /> The followers of Laecanus are anarchs less concerned with politics, but with metaphysics. The Free States are a good thing because it provides them a safe haven to overcome the limitations of the Kindred condition. Of course, what makes the Ordo Dracul an interesting faction in Requiem is that they actually have accomplishments to share. Laecanus and the other Libertas philosophers have nothing but theories. This doesn't mean they are useless as a setting element. Everyone starts from nothing. This is the part of the Requiem setting's Dracula after he abandons his dabblings with Theban Sorcery and Cruac, but before he achieves his first Coil. That can be a compelling setting element even if there is no payoff (ever, or even just in the timeframe of the chronicle). I imagine The Grand Undying King of the Children of Osiris was at this stage before he finally discovered Bardo, or the first vampire to achieve Golconda. So this does have some precedent in the VtM setting as well. This could be part of some characters' Golconda search or story arc.<br /> <br /> Use some of the techniques of the Ordo Dracul for Laecanus and some of his followers (though without the results of the Coils). These will be the small number of devoted ones who truly believe. Have more hangers on that are intrigued, but until they see some benefit won't participate, or perhaps be inconsistent in their participation. More that like what they hear, but are otherwise uninvolved in Laecanus' metaphysics. Then the vast majority that pays no attention or sees them only as crackpots.<br /> <br /> This is certainly not the only thing an ST can do with Laecanus, but right now this is my starting point. By the time I start the actual chronicle, I may end up going in another direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T09:24:44-07:00","id":1550693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1550654#post1550654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a mention of an &quot;evangelical anarch&quot; named Laecanus in the Anarch Cookbook. It's in the same section on philosophy that mentions perspectives on diablerie and Libertas. It's part of the same mess of gnosticism that pervades a lot of early WoD and Vampire. Laecanus proclaims a &quot;new moral perspective&quot; on Caine. Basically, the villain is God and Caine was unjustly punished. Since he was punished unjustly, all vampires are also unjustly punished. That frenzy where you killed all those people? Not your fault. The blame is on God.<br /> <br /> Laecanus believes that is Kindred can just absolve themselves of any guilt, they can free themselves of frenzy since their cause is external. It's just another strange belief that is not supported by game mechanics, but as a philosophy in the setting it does have some internal logic. However, I can't see this as possibly working. Someone who tries to feel no guilt at all is just going to fuel the Beast and let him take over.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of oddball anarch characters mentioned in the Anarch Cookbook and elsewhere, the best place to put this character is in the Free States. It's another missed opportunity of LABN that it did not include him. This is the kind of thing that can make an interesting NPC for the PCs to interact with.<br /> <br /> However, as far as I know there is nothing else known about this character. We get just one paragraph. The most likely clans for him would either be Brujah or Malkavian. His theory is so outlandish it would be easy to just label him Malkavian. However, then it'd be too easy to dismiss in my opinion. The Brujah are supposed to be a clan of philosophers and radical thinkers, and I think this also fits in well with them.<br /> <br /> As &quot;apostle of Caine&quot; brings up connotations of the Path of Caine and thus the Sabbat, but I won't have this character be connected with them. Once you start with the idea that the first vampire was Cain, you are going to have ideas like this pop up independently. Sabbat on the Path of Caine might want to contact such a character if they hear about him, but I would prefer Laecanus to be sincere in his anarch loyalties.</div> </div> </div> </div> I\u2019ll bet that this fellow and Anatole just love each other - the way a rat love the terrier.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I definitely agree that Laecanus should not be a Malkavian - too cliche - and would definitely agree with his being a Brujah (I wonder if his rhetoric is pleased to suggest an Ancient origin for this philosophy - possibly spurious - and if he insists that this is his own creation or attributes the inspiration to some more respected elder?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T11:33:52-07:00","id":1550700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1550693#post1550693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ll bet that this fellow and Anatole just love each other - the way a rat love the terrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure besides Anatole that a lot of other canon characters, like Aristotle de Laurent and Cuthbert Beckett, would challenge his interpretations. And maybe that's a good thing that the anarchs have their own intellectuals who can challenge the leading scholars of the Camarilla. Their arguments are not Maoist insurgencies, but vicious academic office politics of professors with nothing but contempt for the arguments of their rivals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1KQSgcAcNpo\" data-code=\"1KQSgcAcNpo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1KQSgcAcNpo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1550693#post1550693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a more serious note, I definitely agree that Laecanus should not be a Malkavian - too cliche - and would definitely agree with his being a Brujah</div> </div> </div> </div>Most LA Brujah are of the iconoclast stereotype so having a more philosopher type that is still relevant to the anarchs is a welcome addition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1550693#post1550693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I wonder if his rhetoric is pleased to suggest an Ancient origin for this philosophy - possibly spurious - and if he insists that this is his own creation or attributes the inspiration to some more respected elder?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Since gnostic interpretations go way back in both the real world and the World of Darkness, I think it'd be best to acknowledge this is not a new idea. That would also play up the scholarly attributes of the character. The Dark Ages sourcebook provides a lot of past lore like the Cainite Heresy which supports a prior history of &quot;gnostic Caine.&quot; We can use some of that. Of course Laecanus has his own interpretations of any historical lore. He's not going to preach an obsolete heretical religion. <br /> <br /> However, I think it would be interesting for the PCs to hear some old lore through him, and perhaps he's even collected scholarly artifacts like a bad copy of the Euagetaematikon, the old holy text of the Church of Caine, along with other artifacts like partial selections of the Book of Nod, portions of the Erciyes Fragments, and others. That way he's not just some fruitcake, but seems like a real scholar and philosopher. Less of a historian or theologian, and more of a philosopher. Maybe some kind of Hegelian.<br /> <br /> While I cannot find an antecedent for the name of Laecanus, I find in Wikipedia there was a Roman gens called Laecania, and that there are several relatively minor historical figures with the cognomen of Laecanius. The name is likely based on that if it isn't just some random chance. However, there is a Laecanius who was one of the soldiers said to have killed the Emperor Galba in AD 69, the Year of the Four Emperors. That would make a good pseudonym for an anarch in my opinion. It might also be a hint as to his scholarly tastes if he read Tacitus.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, <a href=\"https://www.ebay.com/itm/225923112066\" target=\"_blank\">an internet search just turned up a VTES card of &quot;Laecanus&quot;</a> on eBay that is clearly supposed to be him as the card reads &quot;immune to frenzy.&quot; The card though states he is a Toreador. So it seems this character was recalled by those creating the cards. I don't hold VTES cards to be any kind of canon, but I do find it interesting he was mentioned afterwards!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T03:21:33-07:00","id":1550730,"title":"","content":"It might be amusing to suggest that the confusion between \u2018Laecanus\u2019 and \u2018Laecanius\u2019 arose due to the Kindred being largely self-taught and speaking Latin with an unusual accent (Resulting in \u2018lay-can-ee-us\u2019 becoming \u2018lay-canny-yus\u2019).<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, the idea of Laecanus being a Toreador is quite an intriguing one - perhaps this particular Rose found himself slipping from connoisseur into ideologue after he started being able to read the illuminated manuscripts he had previously collected for the beauty of their illustrations and handwriting?<br /> <br /> If nothing else, a Toreador demagogue with Anarch leanings would have a somewhat easier time walking the line between Camarilla and Free States in the style suggested by the \u2018Camarilla\u2019 on that card (Which would add a new, interesting wrinkle to the character as somebody tightrope-walking along the Frontier), given they would have curiosity value, rather than being regarded as a typical Anarch ranter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their arguments are not Maoist insurgencies, but vicious academic office politics of professors with nothing but contempt for the arguments of their rivals. </div> </div> </div> Doubtless they\u2019re almost equally happy to badmouth their notional allies too, being Revolutionary Academics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-07T19:34:22-07:00","id":1550822,"title":"","content":"This post is about an extremely minor character mentioned in the Anarch Cookbook. &quot;Character&quot; is probably being generous because all it is a brief exchange in letters between Petrodon and this character used as introductory quotes for that book's first chapter. However, they hint at something intriguing which I feel could be an interesting NPC.<br /> <br /> <i>I once again, with the deepest sincerity, ask you to respond to my inquiries. These tensions are not necessary and only serve to endanger us all. If I could understand your grievances, then I could please your case before the Camarilla. Understand this, I am only attempting to save us all. But I cannot do this unless I understand: what do you want? That is all I want to know: what do you want?\u201d</i><br /> - Justicar Petrodon in a letter to Topaz<br /> <br /> <i>Get this first - I am only writing because I am sick of your damn letters. Are you so stupid, or is this another trick of yours? I don\u2019t belong to you or your damn prince - I\u2019m my own person, free and loving it. If you can\u2019t understand why me and my friends don\u2019t like kissing your ass, then maybe you need to quit lickin\u2019 the blood of your elders and learn to think for yourself - so get off my ass!</i><br /> - Topaz in response<br /> <br /> There are some interesting things about this exchange.<ul><li>Why would Petrodon attempt to reach out to this person in the first place? She seems to be someone important enough for him to not only contact, but try to reconcile with the Camarilla.</li> <li>Topaz seems to be a public figure as he could actually send a written letter to her. So her location, or at least a way to send her a letter, seems publicly known. It implies she is in a safe location, but one that Petrodon cannot reach. The LA Free States is an obvious choice of location, perhaps checked into a hotel under real name.</li> <li>Petrodon is concerned with \u201ctensions\u201d that would \u201cendanger\u201d everyone. He only wants to \u201csave\u201d us. What exactly is the danger here?</li> <li>Topaz seems to have committed some crime or at least scandalous action or utterance, but Petrodon thinks he could plead her case. This seems to imply that she has legitimate grievances, and that her crime is perhaps not so severe. Yet if that is the case, why is Petrodon involved at all?</li> <li>Topaz sounds very young and immature in her writing. Not only is she young as a vampire, she seems to have been embraced young as well. She doesn't seem to understand the position of someone like Justicar Petrodon. She seems to imagine he's a flunky to his damn prince, not one of the most important vampires in the world.</li> </ul>\u200bWhile there are multiple ways to imagine this, I believe Topaz is probably a very young childe of some important figure in the Camarilla. A powerful prince perhaps since Topaz mentions &quot;your damn prince&quot;. Maybe she has insider information that could be damaging. Or her defection is just very humiliating for her sire, perhaps weakening him fatally. Or she has not been released under the Tradition of Accounting, and thus her actions could technically cause her sire to be punished. At the same time, this seems more than something that affects just one domain as the matter seems to be something that requires addressing &quot;before the Camarilla.&quot; But what does that mean? Clearly not the Inner Circle. Perhaps to a conclave?<br /> <br /> Such a character might not only be interesting to meet - how many people have correspondence with a Justicar (and given a return address!) - but I feel her situation could easily involve new PCs in actual plot for the game session. Topaz seems totally unimportant. Fairly weak neonate along the lines of new PCs. Nobody important. Someone new PCs could realistically become involved in. Yet they could encounter some real stakes with her. Petrodon (or her sire) could send agents to kidnap her in LA. Perhaps send in ghouls, bribe some local anarchs, hire some disposable Caitiff or other desperate vampire to go LA and retrieve her. They don't even necessarily want to harm her or destroy her (her disposable and unimportant friends though...). Nobody else in the Free States really knows or cares about her. The stakes don't seem high for the PCs initially. They just need to befriend another new arrival and care enough to help her. But they could potentially figure out that some very important people want her their own personal reasons that are very important to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SxZ_xBmBJek\" data-code=\"SxZ_xBmBJek\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/SxZ_xBmBJek/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Of course, all the fun bits still need to be figured out. What's her clan, who's her sire, what dangerous knowledge she possesses, what are her interesting quirks and description? Make her someone that the PCs want to help, and would like after everything is resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T12:59:38-07:00","id":1550852,"title":"","content":"Given that Amethyst and Topaz are both gemstones (Also that the former was embraced at a painfully young age, was strongly associated with the Prince of Baltimore - to the point of being kidnapped by Anarchs in a bid to manipulate same - before the point where she decided to join the very Anarchs who had kidnapped her - since her Prince disappointed her so very thoroughly the Camarilla itself was tainted by association - and given that Amethyst was becoming increasingly prominent in LA at roughly the same time Baltimore was reaching a state of affairs sufficiently delicate that the local Prince simply could not afford to be associated with an Anarch Baron*) I\u2019d suggest that depicting the latter as a sardonic parody of the sort of cloak-and-dagger subtleties a Nosferatu Justicar thrives on but an Anarch might scorn might be the most interesting approach.<br /> <br /> <br /> *A Caitiff Anarch baron at that.<br /> <br /> <br /> If nothing else, a Caitiff Baron locked in a duel with some local rival would seem more than sufficiently pitiable for somebody as fundamentally eager to believe in his own decency &amp; forbearance as Justicar Petrodon to consider them a plausible target for overtures to help him understand where the Anarchs are coming from, possibly with undertones of \u201cYou can come home, if you like\u201d (Not least because she seems sufficiently weak that any scornful response on her part would be seen as childish petulance rather than defiance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-27T17:57:29-07:00","id":1551319,"title":"","content":"I recently found something on the White Wolf Wiki that I am wondering if I should include in some capacity. It concerns some characters in the Chaos Factor sourcebook. I don't own or have access to that sourcebook, so my only information is what is on the wiki. I know its one of the more gonzo sourcebooks which is usually not too my taste, but I'll take inspiration from wherever I find it.<br /> <br /> It concerns two characters that have some tie to the Anarch Free States. The first is <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Delilah_Monroe\" target=\"_blank\">Delilah Monroe</a> and the second is <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mad_Mary\" target=\"_blank\">Mad Mary</a>.<br /> <br /> First, the stuff I like. Delilah was embraced in southern California. She originally joined the Sabbat, but later defected to the Anarchs and made trips to Los Angeles and Seattle to recruit support to overthrow the Sabbat in Mexico City. She's very much a SoCal punk musician in appearance. She'd be a good fit for the chronicle. <br /> <br /> Mad Mary is a Malkavian anti-tribu turned in New York City who somehow made her way to Mexico City. She has Medicine 3 so maybe she was some kind of nurse or doctor back in New York. She knows Delilah and has been convinced by her to go anarch. Presumably she was already someone with Loyalist allegiances. She's tried of being told what to do. Mad Mary isn't a very deep character or have any reason to be affiliated with LA, but her connection with Delilah is good enough. And if she's really interested in the Loyalist cause (even for purely selfish reasons), then it's not that much of a leap to want to defect. Interestingly, while Delilah has Linguistics 1 indicating she probably knows Spanish, Mad Mary has no such skill suggesting she still only knows English. She probably just wants to leave Mexico City just for that.<br /> <br /> Second, the stuff I don't like. Delilah is a Daughter of Cacophony. I will be changing that. I believe if you are going to include a rare bloodline like the Daughters of Cacophony, it should be for the purposes of running a story/plot about the mystery of that bloodline. Otherwise it's just gratuitous. I don't have any plans or interest to do that. Furthermore, there isn't anything that really makes this character a DoC. Delilah could be from any clan, and the character would be just as good (or bad). Delilah could just as easily be a Toreador. I'll probably just make her that. <br /> <br /> It's not clear why exactly she became Sabbat. Presumably her sire wasn't. I imagine she was recruited very early by some Loyalist nomad pack (perhaps with Mad Mary) and quickly found out not all Sabbat was like that aftern she arrived in Mexico City. Perhaps she spent a lot of time on the road with the pack (she was embraced in 1981) and had only recently arrived in Mexico City With weak vinculum she was able to leave, and Mad Mary went with her. (Maybe most of that nomad pack was recently killed, and a new ductus went to Mexico City to recruit more, and that's when she decided to leave.) <br /> <br /> It's also not exactly clear why she would want to go back to Mexico City once she got out. It's not like she has any ties down there. Does she really like Mexico City that much despite the obvious danger there? It makes more sense she'd go to somewhere she knows (SoCal) and wants to be at (the Free States). Obviously, this isn't canon per Chaos Factor, but it'll work for my purposes.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what to do about Delilah's morality being on the Path of Evil Revelations. At least on the Wiki, there's no real justification for it. Is this just another example of gratuitous inclusion of rare lore just to have it? Or is there more to it? Dealing with someone on that Path might be interesting, but it may also just be distracting from the more obvious hooks with the character. Also not sure how Delilah could continue to improve on it without an actual mentor to guide her, and I'm leery to add some minor demon or imp just to do it. Maybe just give her the same Path as Mad Mary (Cathari) or just keep her on the Path of Humanity and assume this version never got to the point of abandoning her default path. There are various musicians who claim to be Satanists just for the shock value, and I'm incline to limit it to just this. I'm open about this question.<br /> <br /> A duo of Sabbat defectors who can bring some knowledge of the Sabbat to the Free States would be useful, and the characters in and of themselves are fine. It aligns of some of what I've already discussed here like anarchs being active in Mexico and various levels of support given to them. Some of the characters we've discussed now have strong ties to Mexico. This just builds on that.<br /> <br /> I also think I can use them to start several plots hooks with the PCs. If they just arrive in the city, the first Kindred they find could be the PCs. The PCs would need to decide what to do. Just eliminate these NPCs as a risk? Talk with established anarch NPCs on what to do? Try to get information out of them before deciding anything? I think this could become something that could fill up a lot of time for one game session or possibly even leading to multiple sessions. It would be a way to introduce more Sabbat plot elements. <br /> <br /> Mad Mary is much more Sabbat mentality than Delilah is, and presumably would have more trouble adjusting to Los Angeles. if the PCs intervene in their favor to be accepted into the Anarchs, it might be interesting to see how they try to mentor Mad Mary and if they are successful or if they just alienate her by always stopping what she wants to do. Delilah would be much easier to integrate, so this is one thing I could do with Mad Mary that I couldn't with Delilah.<br /> <br /> If there's more information on these characters in Chaos Factor that would be relevant, and someone knows it, I'm interested in hearing it. These are very minor characters, but I've already come up with several ideas on how I can use them. Precisely because they are minor, I don't mind if they end up being disposable if the PCs go down that route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T13:15:46-07:00","id":1551350,"title":"","content":"Interesting to note another instance of Seattle being something of a hot spot for Anarch characters popping into Camarilla territory (I believe that Germaine is also noted to have paid a visit at some point, apparently running afoul of Petrodon) despite the city being Base of Operations for a Camarilla Justicar.<br /> <br /> Makes you wonder if, at some point in his not-so-recent history Petrodon was more interested in exploiting the Free States against the Sabbat than in stamping out the Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T17:50:20-07:00","id":1551356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1551350#post1551350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting to note another instance of Seattle being something of a hot spot for Anarch characters popping into Camarilla territory (I believe that Germaine is also noted to have paid a visit at some point, apparently running afoul of Petrodon) despite the city being Base of Operations for a Camarilla Justicar.</div> </div> </div> </div>The early sourcebooks tended to mention that while Oregon and Washington states were considered Camarilla loyal, that there were substantial anarchs there. We could interpret that to mean that there was a deliberate strategy by the anarchs to try to control the entire west coast. Probably because of geographic ease, but controlling the entire west coast would also have several obvious advantages. That could also be another reason San Francisco's &quot;neutrality&quot; is respected by the Free States. It would make a good place for Kindred from the Pacific Northwest to meet up and exchange favors or materials with the Kindred of SoCal. Going to San Francisco is not as suspicious as going to Los Angeles. Attacking San Fran (and worse, then failing) would jeopardize that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-09T08:52:48-07:00","id":1551539,"title":"","content":"I wonder how Petrodon himself would exploit that clearing-house after escalating his operations against the Free States, possibly after provocation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T15:43:28-07:00","id":1552392,"title":"","content":"A very old canon character is Ehrich Weiss, who we know better by his stage name Harry Houdini. In canon, he was embraced without permission by a 10th generation Tremere, but was accepted anyway by the Tremere Inner Circle and blood bonded to them (note: in 1e, Tremere characters were fully blood bonded to the Inner Circle, not just partial). While in real life Houdini died in 1926, canon seems to state that he was embraced in 1926, but kept performing (though only at night) publicly until 1930 when he staged his death. Not sure why this would be the case. Did the writer just get his facts wrong? Or was this an attempt to show how the WoD's history is altered from our own? Anyway, Houdini managed to destroy his blood bond and then disappeared, travelling the world in secret while Clan Tremere attempted to hunt him as a rogue.<br /> <br /> One time when he was in Chicago, he met Tracy Graves (Erichtho) whom he had known previously through written correspondence, and discovered she was also a Tremere vampire. She concealed his secret (because she was not blood bonded to the Inner Circle, but Nicolai). Whatever he did to break his blood bond does not seem to work for others, as he is still trying to figure out how to break Tracy's bond. Ehrich still travels around the world, but would visit Chicago at least twice a year and became indirectly involved in Anarch politics there because of Tracy. For our purposes, I don't need to go into further detail.<br /> <br /> While the biography of vampire character of Ehrich Weiss never mentions Los Angeles, we know the real life Houdini briefly live there in 1919 while filming some movies, and his wife later moved back there after his death. I think his wife lived there until she died in 1943, but travelled much between there and New York City. I also have to think that even someone constantly travelling the world does need to take a break every now and again. And if he's willing to to be predictable enough to visit Chicago twice a year to see his friend/correspondent Tracy Graves then he's not adverse at stopping over at the same city time and again.<br /> <br /> Plus if you are a rogue Tremere constantly hunted by the clan, why wouldn't you utilize the California Free States? The Tremere don't hold power there, and if he has anarch sympathies, it makes sense.<br /> <br /> So I am putting LA as a place that Ehrich Weiss extensively visits. He doesn't involve himself in politics and stays away from rants or other public appearances. Despite his anarch sympathies, his real passion (in the WoD as a vampire) is exploring the afterlife and the occult. He just needs a place he can relax for a while before moving on (much like Germaine and other well travelled Kindred who are not aligned with the Camarilla). I imagine the most important vampires in LA do know of him, but respect his privacy.<br /> <br /> I imagine he is in contact with the more serious or learned mystical or occult oriented anarchs in LA (and perhaps magi and sorcerers as well). Any contact with the PCs will need to come through their involvement in that scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T17:47:32-07:00","id":1552395,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Weiss stays at The Magic Castle when in LA?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T12:38:27-07:00","id":1552423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1552395#post1552395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps Weiss stays at The Magic Castle when in LA?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting enough LA landmark that it could be used productively in any chronicle. I'll need to keep this location in mind.<br /> <br /> However, I'll probably have Ehrich avoid it. He might be too recognizable there, and while a stage musician and escapologist in life, he's clearly moved on to other pursuits. So little reward and some risk. (Likewise he probably avoids the so-called Houdini Mansion/Estate at Laurel Canyon.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T14:14:17-07:00","id":1552427,"title":"","content":"Given his longtime quest of (allegedly) trying to find a real psychic to communicate with his dead mother, one can't help but wonder Weiss's reaction to the existence of the Necromancy discipline. \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I always thought that a bunch of stage magicians and mentalists would have made for a cool Hunters Hunted faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T04:48:46-07:00","id":1552447,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a>, Especially if those illusionists and mentalists are working in the same ghost-breaking spirit as the late Ehrich Weiss (I.E. seeking out those exploiting the more credulous and thoroughly exposing them) then they would make excellent opponents for Mages or Changelings, for whom belief and conviction are so important.<br /> <br /> I suspect they would be a tad squishy for a Vampire or Werewolf campaign (Unless being backed by somebody with actual supernatural Juice).<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I suspect that Mr Weiss wouod have to be very careful about visiting LA when his wife was in residence: one can imagine a very classic Urban Fantasy dilemma centring on the man missing his lady, but feeling deeply reluctant to disillusion her hopes that he Rests in Peace.<br /> <br /> Also, \u2018Vampire Houdini\u2019 is one of those little \u2018World of Darkness as pure Gothic Pulp\u2019 details that brings a little smile to my face (It occurs to me that the historic Houdini\u2019s fascination with the line between Life &amp; Death make him a very natural enemy of the Giovanni - who abuse it so - and a useful complication for a Wraith campaign).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T11:28:13-07:00","id":1552454,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> the original Hunters Hunted had Dennis Quincy, &quot;The Uncanny Danny&quot; who I'm pretty sure was intended as an homage to James &quot;the Amazing&quot; Randi. He'd be perfect as a leader of illusionist/mentalist hunters.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a> It's a bit unfortunate for a LA chronicle that Houdini's wife died (1943) prior to the revolt against Don Sebastian (1944). If Ehrich ever visited her in secret, it would have been done when Sebastian still ruled, and thus has a high chance of any LA Tremere observing her in case Ehrich ever showed up. So he doesn't have much of an emotional stake in LA itself. I see him mostly as using LA as a convenient spot because it lacks any official chantry. Ehrich may have some anarch sympathies, but he doesn't seem to be an enemy of the Camarilla in general.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Giovanni and the Necromany discipline, I will note that Ehrich's (sole?) appearance in 1991's Succubus Club predates even the 1e Players Guide (where the Giovanni and Necromancy made their first appearance). A future &quot;Ghost&quot; game line was already planned, but there was literally nothing that character or story could refer to in terms of actual vampire powers. His Disciplines are rather low key - only Auspex 2, Dominate 2, Movement of Mind 3, and Lure of Flames 1. A more recent rendition of the character would probably expand on his powers.<br /> <br /> Character knowledge of both Thaumaturgy and Necromancy have expanded greatly from the early game. Given Ehrich's interest, it would make sense a world travelling rogue Tremere seeking occult knowledge would have picked up some actual wraith lore and necromancy in terms of how the game portrays the setting today. Since LA lacks any real representation of either Tremere or Giovanni, I imagine it must have other &quot;occult refugees&quot; looking for a place without either clan. They could be part of some occult coterie (whose members might belong to other coteries as well) with whom Ehrich stays in contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T12:39:15-07:00","id":1552459,"title":"","content":"The Uncanny Danny and Deborah Rose Keller are both characters I think could have easily been expanded into groups. In the case of Danny, probably this mix skeptics who have seen something they can't (yet) explain and of people who want to find something paranormal but are very wary of fakes.<br /> <br /> I'll also note that Houdini wrote a book called The Right Way to Do Wrong, a collection of short essays detailing how he did some of his escapes, exposing tricks used by rivals, and (perhaps most interesting for an Anarch campaign) discussing his interviews with various policemen and criminals and his thoughts on how to commit crimes without getting caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T12:59:32-07:00","id":1552460,"title":"","content":"At some point in the Crossovers thread, I intend to get to Hunters. I'll probably address both of those characters. James Randi was a frequent guest on Johnny Carson and other TV shows debunking the paranormal so the Uncanny Danny could take his place. Might be a good use of the Magic Castle to have it be home to a secret group of atheist, scientifically inclined hunters trying to figure out a materialist explanation for vampires. Deborah Rose Keller explicitly lives in California. She seems very Orange County to me. As a public advocate investigating occult related crimes and highly skilled in investigation, she'd be another interesting antagonist. As you said, it's natural both would have some kind of organization (especially in the case of Keller).<br /> <br /> Showing a large variety of local hunters, something that is a result of not having an obvious Prince-like figure doing the hard work of maintaining the Masquerade, would be another &quot;feature&quot; of the Free States. <br /> <br /> What will be more of a challenge for me is running hunter plots that do not rely on a direct confrontation with the PCs, but working around them. I find hunter plots to be the least fun and successful plots in Vampire because ultimately if you run the hunters smart, the PCs will get destroyed during the daytime, and if you run them dumb so the PCs live, I find it a waste and the players don't have fun in either scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-18T11:52:58-07:00","id":1552517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1552454#post1552454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> the original Hunters Hunted had Dennis Quincy, &quot;The Uncanny Danny&quot; who I'm pretty sure was intended as an homage to James &quot;the Amazing&quot; Randi. He'd be perfect as a leader of illusionist/mentalist hunters.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a> It's a bit unfortunate for a LA chronicle that Houdini's wife died (1943) prior to the revolt against Don Sebastian (1944). If Ehrich ever visited her in secret, it would have been done when Sebastian still ruled, and thus has a high chance of any LA Tremere observing her in case Ehrich ever showed up. So he doesn't have much of an emotional stake in LA itself. I see him mostly as using LA as a convenient spot because it lacks any official chantry. Ehrich may have some anarch sympathies, but he doesn't seem to be an enemy of the Camarilla in general.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Giovanni and the Necromany discipline, I will note that Ehrich's (sole?) appearance in 1991's Succubus Club predates even the 1e Players Guide (where the Giovanni and Necromancy made their first appearance). A future &quot;Ghost&quot; game line was already planned, but there was literally nothing that character or story could refer to in terms of actual vampire powers. His Disciplines are rather low key - only Auspex 2, Dominate 2, Movement of Mind 3, and Lure of Flames 1. A more recent rendition of the character would probably expand on his powers.<br /> <br /> Character knowledge of both Thaumaturgy and Necromancy have expanded greatly from the early game. Given Ehrich's interest, it would make sense a world travelling rogue Tremere seeking occult knowledge would have picked up some actual wraith lore and necromancy in terms of how the game portrays the setting today. Since LA lacks any real representation of either Tremere or Giovanni, I imagine it must have other &quot;occult refugees&quot; looking for a place without either clan. They could be part of some occult coterie (whose members might belong to other coteries as well) with whom Ehrich stays in contact.</div> </div> </div> </div> If not a full coterie then you can bet there would be a grapevine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-24T23:30:34-07:00","id":1552641,"title":"","content":"I've decided to add another canon character. I already had designated a character as &quot;pornographer&quot;, but that was merely intended as filler. A placeholder for an unimportant character I might bring in whenever I needed someone in the scene because the PCs did something unexpected. I am slotting Derrick Zeel from the 1e Clanbook Toreador into that role.<br /> <br /> However, I will be ignoring the idea that he's actually the fourth generation methusaleh Iontius. While Iontius is mentioned as one possibility for Zeel's real identity, I always took that as one possible option among the many rumors told about him. It was all up to the ST. I know that officially became canon when the authors decided the illustrator of the Encyclopedia Vampirica had to be Iontius and confirmed Zeel was him, but I don't like that for various reasons. I also know they made Iontius be from San Francisco, and I'll be ignoring that too.<br /> <br /> The original write up says &quot;gangs of powerful anarchs surround him and keep other Kindred from bothing him&quot;. To me, that pretty much cements that he should be from the Free States. Where else are there going to be gangs of powerful anarchs? Furthermore, if &quot;few have actually seen him in person&quot;, why would he have multiple gangs of anarchs explicitly protecting him? Wouldn't they have met him? So my interpretation is that he's just a reclusive Toreador, and the &quot;gangs&quot; protecting him are just a reference to the Los Angeles anarchs in general.<br /> <br /> Now Los Angeles is not the only place a pornographer could be. The industry has been split up into several locations, but I think Los Angeles (specifically the San Fernando Valley) has been dominant since the seventies, and is about to experience a boom in the nineties (my chronicle will begin in 1992). So placing Zeel in LA is a no brainer for me.<br /> <br /> &quot;Derrick Zeel&quot; is simply a stage name, like Dirk Diggler. In the rare times he actually sees another Kindred, he'll be called that too, but no one believes it's a real name. While Clanbook Toreador says Zeel &quot;owns&quot; the video production company that makes his films, I'll be taking that to mean he controls the company. Actual ownership would likely entail a situation where any enterprising investigator could determine Zeel's real name. Although that could lead to a scenario where the &quot;real person&quot; Zeel is impersonating is a deceased child whose SSN he could use, I think the danger of that being exposed would just create too many liabilities.<br /> <br /> There's a few things that make the reclusive porn star someone whom PCs might encounter. The first is that he's &quot;a major figure in the slave trade&quot;, which I assume is similar to the &quot;auction&quot; done by the ghoul Williams in the Forged in Steel setting of Gary, IN contained in the 1e and 2e corebooks. Except that it is much, much larger in scale. The porn industry (and LA in general) just has access to a lot of &quot;disposable&quot; people that won't be missed. Zeel's &quot;slave trade&quot; offers a lot of mentally/emotionally/physically broken mortals as slaves to be used by Kindred willing to pay Zeel. I imagine there are various anarchs who have Herds courtesy of Zeel's slave trade, and this may be the reason why &quot;gangs of powerful anarchs&quot; would protect him.<br /> <br /> While mostly based in LA itself, it can accommodate anyone in the entirety of the Free States. And he also controls some additional outlets in Camarilla domains like San Francisco, and indirectly traffics people to other domains. I imagine William's Auction in Gary is in contact with it, even if it is mostly local dregs Williams sells. In order to feed this machine, Zeel is likely already involved in the mortal sex trafficking. While this includes a pipeline from Latin America through Mexico (and I may utilize the crime cartel controlled by the Zantosa Revenants that I stated in the Sabbat thread), it also includes ocean traffic through the ports which requires an agreement with David Geduld.<br /> <br /> The second is the idea that Zeel has &quot;cults dedicated to him in every corner of the world.&quot; Does this mean it's an extremely large and expansive blood cult? Is he some kind of erotic Adonis or Tammuz like figure who's revived a neopagan cult dedicated to him? (Note that if we assume Arikel would be identified with Venus/Aphrodite/Ishtar/Inanna, then Zeel's identification with Adonis might make some believe he must secretly be a childe of the Toreador antediluvian.) If this Adonis-like cult is worldwide, it is highly likely the vampire established it BEFORE he &quot;became&quot; Derrick Zeel, and his worldwide cult simply recognized him in his porn films (which again, may lead to rumors that he is a far older vampire). Or something else? Does this worldwide cult somehow feed into his extensive slave trade? Does Zeel travel a lot to maintain the cult (or perhaps just sends out ghouls to do so)?<br /> <br /> I will make the &quot;one Thaumaturgist&quot; who claims Zeel is Iontius, an anarch Thaumaturgist. He's onto Zeels' real identity, much like Charlie is onto Pepe Silvia. (I may have to name that anarch thaumaturgist Barney.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_nTpsv9PNqo\" data-code=\"_nTpsv9PNqo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_nTpsv9PNqo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> This gives me a lot to work with, and multiple ways I could introduce new NPCs and plot hooks to the PCs depending on what they intend to do.<br /> <br /> Concentrating on these plot hooks do a lot more for me as an ST running a Free State chronicle than making him Iontius. I really don't need another powerful Toreador methusaleh in LA. So whatever others may do, this is what I am going with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-25T11:14:47-07:00","id":1552646,"title":"","content":"<br /> The &quot;X is actually an ancient Methuselah&quot; feels like a well early Vampire kept going back to more often than necessary. \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Regarding Zeel's widespread blood cult and not having it be so obviously traced back to him and his porn company, perhaps it operates as the secret inner circle of a hedonistic underground sex cult. Something that combines stuff from certain episodes of Law &amp; Order: SVU and Eyes Wide Shut. Under such a sex cult, Zeel may be known by a totally different identity. And just personally, it would amuse me if said identity was &quot;The King of Skin&quot; or something equally over-the-top ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if you wanted to have something really weird (and very 90s) to lead back to Zeel, there is always the world of local &quot;indy fed&quot; professional wrestling. Between about 1995 and 2000, there was a San Francisco based promotion called Incredibly Strange Wrestling that operated out of a single venue and did shows that were a mix of luche libre style wrestling matches and performances by local punk, psychobilly, and thrash metal bands. The from 1999 to 2002, there was Xtreme Pro Wrestling in Los Angeles. Clearly trying to do what ECW had done in Philadelphia, it focused on hardcore/deathmatch style wrestling. What makes XPW quasi-memorable is that it was founded and run by a pr0n actor/producer, with both him and various talent appearing regularly in the promotion.<br /> I think it would be easy to combine the two ideas into a single promotion; one started by Zeel as perhaps a way to entertain younger LA area Anarchs and perhaps endear himself to them. The early 90s (especially 1995) was essentially the nadir of American pro wrestling between its two major boom periods, but it did still have its local die hards, especially in parts of southern California, and 96 and 97 would see the start of its resurgence. Something that starts around 94 or 95 as this totally underground thing of local music acts interspersed with exhibitions of Mexican luche libre and Japanese deathmatch wrestling, eventually growing into the WoD's version of ECW, full of ultraviolence and sleezy sex appeal, thanks in no small part to Zeel's ability to get them PPV access. <br /> <br /> At any rate, such a thing would be a good excuse to have an appearance by El Diablo Verde. And even the sort of thing the Fake Rapper archetype from the original Brujah clanbook might find himself involved in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-25T13:36:43-07:00","id":1552648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs?p=1552646#post1552646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Zeel's widespread blood cult and not having it be so obviously traced back to him and his porn company, perhaps it operates as the secret inner circle of a hedonistic underground sex cult. Something that combines stuff from certain episodes of Law &amp; Order: SVU and Eyes Wide Shut. Under such a sex cult, Zeel may be known by a totally different identity. And just personally, it would amuse me if said identity was &quot;The King of Skin&quot; or something equally over-the-top ridiculous</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it should be under a different name too which is why I wondered if it should be established before the identity of &quot;Derrick Zeel&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think it's a fairly simple thing if the cult is local and based around Zeel. That is probably just a typical blood cult. However, a worldwide cult is something else entirely. If he is in LA (or whatever location the ST wants him in), then what benefit can he get from cult members in Sydney, Australia; Hamburg, Germany; Buenos Aires, Argentina; and so on? It certainly isn't blood.<br /> <br /> Now if he was Iontius (which I am not using in my chronicles), and Iontius can &quot;feed&quot; somehow on sexual energy instead of blood, maybe that somehow can get transmitted long distance? However, I really don't like that as a concept, even for a fourth generation methusaleh vampire. So I won't be using it for Zeel who I imagine may still be of some potent blood and perhaps at least an ancillae, but still nowhere near in power for an ancient methusaleh.<br /> <br /> The worldwide cult has to be part of some long term plan even if it is just something mundane like making sure he has available herds should he relocate somewhere. However, that still requires some amount of management and effort, and that's a lot of resources being used now for something that does not provide immediate benefits. Does he visit them through astral projection via Auspex? Does he have an elder power of Presence that can be effective over long distance (even if limited in other scopes)? Just send ghouls out every now and again?<br /> <br /> Is the cult somehow magical in nature? By that I mean its practitioners may learn some form of sorcery (at least the most talented members)? If so, that may explain why one &quot;Thaumaturgist&quot; believes Zeel is Iontius. Maybe he was involved at some point with Zeel's cult, either to learn their version of mortal magic, or trying to help them learn a sorcery version of his paths, and then witnessed something he thought was evidence of Zeel's age and power? Could it be infernalist in nature?<br /> <br /> Is the cult male centered (like his porno audience would likely be) or female centered (like a cult of Adonis/Tammuz would likely be) or appeals to both sexes equally?<br /> <br /> Regardless, what is the cult doing that benefits him? There has to be a plan, and there has to be a goal. It doesn't even need to be his - in typical VtM fashion, perhaps he is just a pawn of another vampire (Iontius slumbering in torpor somewhere?).<br /> <br /> I am leaning to a cult based on Adonis/Tammuz simply because of its natural ties to an Aphrodite/Inanna figure whom would naturally be Arikel. Maybe the cult is truly directed towards her, but an Adonis-like figure is a useful intermediary. That might make it some kind of well hidden Gehenna cult, but specifically on behalf of one antediluvian, not to them in general. Of course, that would be something that could only be revealed to someone deep into the cult. There'd be several layers to pierce before anyone from the oustide would get proof of that. On the surface it just appears to be various sex cults connected to a local LA blood cult with some occult mumbo jumbo.<br /> <br /> It can be nebulous enough so that NPCs and players may never know and can pick one option of a confusing mess of what it could be. As long as the ST knows what its true purpose is, she'll know how to portray it and run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-25T17:16:00-07:00","id":1552650,"title":"","content":"The southern California part of the cult may be a competitor/rival to Jack Parsons group back in the 1940s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}